{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane","id":849587,"title":"Fixing what I dislike about the Gangrel Clan Bane","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-18T20:29:20-07:00","id":849587,"title":"Fixing what I dislike about the Gangrel Clan Bane","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I recently determined exactly what I like, and don't like, about the different clan banes. I want a clan's bane to reinforce their stereotype when a clan member avoids that bane. I want vampires specifically to NOT have to actually suffer the penalties of their banes, and I want the actions they take in avoiding that bane to define them to a degree.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Case in point: I like the Daeva flaw because it causes Daeva to be &quot;promiscuous&quot; with their Kiss. They can't maintain a herd at all (either you never drink twice so you don't suffer Dependency, or you drink exactly twice and then can't anymore without constant Humanity 3 breaking points for causing harm to your regnant), so, they become, metaphorically, whores. That's perfect. So, they can totally avoid the curse by fulfilling their stereotype.<br /> <br /> The Mekhet, too. They have a weird, unique bane. It's a quirk they have to avoid triggering, <i>and</i> avoid letting anyone else know about it so they can't use it against you. This makes Mekhet secretive and quirky. Boom, perfect.<br /> <br /> The Daeva, Mekhet, and Nosferatu flaw all work &quot;correctly&quot; in this regard. I have another thread about touchstones and a stop gap solution for Ventrue. So, that leaves Gangrel. The Gangrel flaw is just not to my preference. The Gangrel are supposed to be wild and bestial, but their flaw, the way you avoid it, is by doing exactly the opposite of that, by maintaining humanity, avoiding anger and anger inducing situations, being extremely polite and nice to everyone to avoid provocations, feeding carefully to keep from hunger, etc., etc. It's everything a Gangrel shouldn't be.<br /> <br /> So, how do we fix this? Well, I'm hoping for some help in that regard. Most suggestions I've seen on the forum for a Gangrel fix are to give them a penalty to resist frenzy, rather than their humanity as a cap, usually at the same rate vampires suffer social penalties from having low humanity. This is definitely better than the book's version, but it still doesn't address my specific problems. Can we do better?<br /> <br /> I was thinking I had to do something that penalized not acting bestial, so they chose to act that way to avoid it. Unfortunately, anything on that front I can think of is problematic. I don't want to penalize them for maintaining Humanity--I want high humanity to remain a pure positive. I considered somehow giving them the Tempted condition in situations that didn't necessarily call for a frenzy check (say, when they had to be excessively patient or something, I don't know), but then, I realized the only way to clear that was to frenzy, and frenzy is kind of a loss condition and isn't fun for all players, so, that's no good.<br /> <br /> I considered maybe playing with the three lashing out conditions. I already remove the month time limit on them, though removing that from just the Gangrel could also be in order, but, nothing I came up with on that front was satisfying, either, because, again, you basically clear those conditions by losing, by facing a breaking point, or for Bestial, hurting someone, which is probably going to be a breaking point anyway.<br /> <br /> I don't want to drive them to frenzy, exactly, but I want them to be aggressive, to prefer the outdoors, to stalk prey, act quickly, that kind of stuff. I don't know.<br /> <br /> Maybe something with willpower, where they can only spend it in certain ways or they have to spend it to do certain things (long term planning?).<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any other ideas? I would appreciate it.<br /> <br /> Let me give some quick parameters on the fix, though, so people don't get frustrated. If you don't know me from my other thread on touchstones, I don't like what we'll call, for lack of a better term, story-game mechanics. I remove or seriously downplay in my games touchstones, Mask/Dirge, aspirations, the way beats are handed out, and the door-based social system, so, please don't root the fix in those systems or make it another directly story altering system in and of itself. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  clarity 03-18-2016, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T21:34:42-07:00","id":849604,"title":"","content":"Desired Behavior: <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">'The Gangrel are supposed to be wild and bestial'<br /> <br /> Repackaged as a positive: 'The Gangrel are supposed to be free and simple/direct.' I.e Wild calls to mind a lack of rules, so free here is freedom from, and Bestial refers to a savage, primitive nature.<br /> <br /> Create Binary for modeling purposes: Freedom from vs Regulated. Simple/direct vs complex/convoluted.<br /> <br /> Theory: Avoiding the binary behavior encourages the desired behavior.<br /> <br /> Seed for Bane: Give Gangrel the tempted condition whenever they are subject to 'micromanagement' or excessive regulation, or when following a course that is more complex than a possible alternative.<br /> <br /> Presumed behavior: Obligation and submission treated with caution; action favored over diplomacy, short term over long term. Failure to maintain freedom and bestiality increases likelihood of frenzy, further reinforcing the stereotype.<br /> <br /> Optional refinement: Tie humanity to sensitivity of micromanagement and complexity. High humanity enables greater tolerance. As such, low humanity Gangrel are more blunt and independent and more prone to frenzy at impediments.<br /> <br /> Refine bane: Triggers are grouped into three: Faceless rules, proscription of methods, and delaying action to optimize. Faceless rules are laws, traditions, and rules that are not directly enforced. The Prince barking an order doesn't tempt; a ghoul informing them that Havens need to be above ground does. Proscription of method occurs when one is told how to accomplish a goal AND forced to comply. Example: Being told to talk to the Sheriff before starting to track the Perp. Forbidden from using excessive force. Delaying action to optimize occurs when it is possible to achieve a goal or satisfy a desire but action is delayed to accomplish some secondary objective. Examples: Talking with the union over contract particulars instead of breaking the strike by force.<br /> <br /> Conclusion: Gangrel are Tempted whenever they must deal with Faceless rules and regulation, when they are made to do something according to specific instruction, or when they must delay the completing of goals or satisfaction of desire.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:09:52-07:00","id":849699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane#post849587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe play with how Willpower can be spent for extra effort? If the action that is being spent on isn't within the Gangrel wheelhouse (something the character might do while frenzied) - rather than a (+3/+2) bonus, they receive (+1) and gain the Tempted (-1) condition (stacks).<br /> <br /> I know you don't use beats in the base way, but I'd also include that Gangrel never receive a beat for resolving the Tempted condition (if there is a way other characters can get beats for conditions. If not, ignore.)<br /> <br /> In theory this should:<ul><li>Show that Gangrel can only reach their full potential when they are working with the beast rather than on things the beast doesn't care about.</li> <li>Encourage Gangrel to frequent places where they can frenzy more often. This is either the wilderness, where frenzies of nature won't be a risk to the Masquerade, or in Kindred controlled places - i.e. among other undead predators.</li> </ul>I thought about playing around with the Bestial aspect. Like, Gangrel could trade their current stack of Tempted Conditions in exchange for the Bestial Condition (number of nights = Tempted penalty), but the (-2) Defense in Bestial makes me stop. I don't think Gangrel should be easier to hit/kill because they are acting on predatory impulses.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you feel about Pack/Dominance themes, you could also play with Teamwork. Gangrel can only benefit from Teamwork when in a Pack situation, or from someone they have successfully lashed out against (i.e. have lower-d dominated).<br /> <br /> Can mess with resisting Frenzy if you are using the new rules for that. Most characters fight against frenzy via resisting the beast obviously, gaining one turn of 'freedom' (hiss, growl, smash a chair) per WP until they stop spending, then get a (+1) per WP spent and a roll at that time. Could say for Gangrel they don't get Freedom for a turn, but still act as if frenzied even while they are spending WP. Or just that they can't spend WP to resist Frenzy at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":".  Wrong person quoted 03-19-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:12:14-07:00","id":849701,"title":"","content":"The idea here is great, but the implementation is exactly what I struggled with. The flaw is so, well, vague. Now, I'm not opposed to judgment calls, but this would be a little excessive. Even trying to explain to someone what a &quot;faceless&quot; rule is, is complicated (mind you, I understand what you mean, but it's not a simple concept) and some rules might appear unenforceble even if they're not. Your set up is exactly what I am looking for, though. They should act directly and unfettered. It's just that the behaviors you identified to &quot;punish&quot; are too vague and disparate to make for an elegant flaw. It feels like just throwing a bunch of stuff together, and it is exactly what I had trouble with, too.<br /> <br /> Maybe we can reach a satisfactory bane by refining it down to a single concept instead of many? Perhaps, following the preview of the Beast Changeling Kith's lead, Gangrel rail against &quot;Confinement,&quot; which applies not just in the physical sense. I feel like that concept might be less specific than your threefold list, but, at the same time, somehow less vague and easier to understand.<br /> <br /> So, penciled in, lets say, &quot;Once per scene, Gangrel suffer from the Tempted condition when they feel Confined. This is not purely physical and applies equally to actual restraints, seemingly pointless rules, and stifling social obligations. The proscription against violence at Elysium, and other such rules do not normally trigger this feeling of Confinement.&quot;<br /> <br /> However, I'd still rather avoid periodic Frenzy as the only way out of their predicament. I wonder if there's another way to generate this same goal? Do I need to directly fix the Tempted condition so that there's another way to resolve it? Do I need to give them a different condition? Bestial perhaps? Or require that they Lash Out against those confining them or it costs them something? Hmm...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 03-19-2016, 10:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T08:28:20-07:00","id":849728,"title":"","content":"Noting that I don't know Vampire <i>at all</i> and was basically browsing the forum out of curiosity: have you considered writing a Condition specifically for this bane? That way you might be able to get a double-whammy - they have to act bestial or reject fetters and constraints to avoid it, and you can write a condition that further encourages that behaviour and is lost when they really play it up.<br /> <br /> Could even go with &quot;lose this condition when you frenzy or [other desirable I'm A Barely-Constrained Beast type action&quot; so that option's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T08:36:48-07:00","id":849732,"title":"","content":"I'd go with having the player decide on one or more trigger that when encountered would give the gangrel character a condition akin to frenzy but with more control (i suck on the mechanical side of things so the goal is act savage but it shouldnt be limited to mindlessly attacking . <br /> The example triggers here could be the usual like violence, pain, hunger. but could be more personnalized like ; the moon, lies, rats, whistles, bells, etc.<br /> The point here is to emphasize savage reaction but still allow for a certain measure of customization. <br /> Not sure if avoiding the circumstances of the bane would emphasize the gangrel archetype tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:17:18-07:00","id":850017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane#post849587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Case in point: I like the Daeva flaw because it causes Daeva to be &amp;quot;promiscuous&amp;quot; with their Kiss. They can't maintain a herd at all (either you never drink twice so you don't suffer Dependency, or you drink exactly twice and then can't anymore without constant Humanity 3 breaking points for causing harm to your regnant), so, they become, metaphorically, whores. That's perfect. So, they can totally avoid the curse by fulfilling their stereotype.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always assumed they can still drink from their Herd, just not so deeply it &quot;injures&quot; (3 health boxes) them. Have I been wrong about this? I know each BP taken does that much superficial Health boxes damage, but it's a bit silly they become obsessed with them yet can't feed at all, isn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:19:43-07:00","id":850019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=849699#post849699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe play with how Willpower can be spent for extra effort? If the action that is being spent on isn't within the Gangrel wheelhouse (something the character might do while frenzied) - rather than a (+3/+2) bonus, they receive (+1) and gain the Tempted (-1) condition (stacks).[<br /> <br /> In theory this should:<ul><li>Show that Gangrel can only reach their full potential when they are working with the beast rather than on things the beast doesn't care about.</li> <li>Encourage Gangrel to frequent places where they can frenzy more often. This is either the wilderness, where frenzies of nature won't be a risk to the Masquerade, or in Kindred controlled places - i.e. among other undead predators.</li> </ul>I thought about playing around with the Bestial aspect. Like, Gangrel could trade their current stack of Tempted Conditions in exchange for the Bestial Condition (number of nights = Tempted penalty), but the (-2) Defense in Bestial makes me stop. I don't think Gangrel should be easier to hit/kill because they are acting on predatory impulses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is kind of what has stymied me as well. Bestial isn't quite right, and frenzying is perhaps too harsh to encourage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=849699#post849699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on how you feel about Pack/Dominance themes, you could also play with Teamwork. Gangrel can only benefit from Teamwork when in a Pack situation, or from someone they have successfully lashed out against (i.e. have lower-d dominated).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be ok with that, but, there's kind of already a Pack Alpha merit with similar themes, and I honestly don't think teamwork comes up enough to justify a bane entirely devoted to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=849699#post849699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can mess with resisting Frenzy if you are using the new rules for that. Most characters fight against frenzy via resisting the beast obviously, gaining one turn of 'freedom' (hiss, growl, smash a chair) per WP until they stop spending, then get a (+1) per WP spent and a roll at that time. Could say for Gangrel they don't get Freedom for a turn, but still act as if frenzied even while they are spending WP. Or just that they can't spend WP to resist Frenzy at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am using 2nd edition in pretty much every way except for Anchors, beats, and doors, so, yeah, I'm using that (which is very similar to 1e anyway, if I recall), but, like I said, I don't want to force frenzy on Gangrel all the time, that's the issue, I want them to be wild and unfettered, but not constantly out of control.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=849728#post849728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Noting that I don't know Vampire <i>at all</i> and was basically browsing the forum out of curiosity: have you considered writing a Condition specifically for this bane? That way you might be able to get a double-whammy - they have to act bestial or reject fetters and constraints to avoid it, and you can write a condition that further encourages that behaviour and is lost when they really play it up.<br /> <br /> Could even go with &quot;lose this condition when you frenzy or [other desirable I'm A Barely-Constrained Beast type action&quot; so that option's there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think that's a good idea, but, well, I'm having trouble doing that. I'm hoping for some good ideas on how to write such a condition, on how to properly word the restrictions/penalties/whatever to make it happen without falling into the &quot;they frenzy a lot&quot; trap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=849732#post849732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd go with having the player decide on one or more trigger that when encountered would give the gangrel character a condition akin to frenzy but with more control (i suck on the mechanical side of things so the goal is act savage but it shouldnt be limited to mindlessly attacking .<br /> The example triggers here could be the usual like violence, pain, hunger. but could be more personnalized like ; the moon, lies, rats, whistles, bells, etc.<br /> The point here is to emphasize savage reaction but still allow for a certain measure of customization.<br /> Not sure if avoiding the circumstances of the bane would emphasize the gangrel archetype tho.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the idea, and it is interesting to play with the idea of giving the player a choice as to what form their wildness takes, but I think, given my goal of getting them to act wild to <i>avoid</i> the penalty, it doesn't quite work. Being forced into this state would certainly be the penalty, so, the standard Gangrel wouldn't be &quot;howling at the moon&quot; (just as an example of the moon causing this state), they'd be constantly looking down away from the moon, or staying indoors, waiting to go outside only when cloudy. If they psuedo frenzy around violence, you'd have Gandhi Gangrel refusing to get involved in conflicts that might lead to violence and trigger them.<br /> <br /> It certainly is tricky. Part of the problem, I'm sure, is that I don't really like the feel of the Gangrel (though I have several players who love the savage/bestial aspects they are designed to play up), so, to me, acting wild and stuff already feels like a penalty. I'm trying, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  typo 03-20-2016, 12:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T21:27:13-07:00","id":850020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850017#post850017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always assumed they can still drink from their Herd, just not so deeply it &quot;injures&quot; (3 health boxes) them. Have I been wrong about this? I know each BP taken does that much superficial Health boxes damage, but it's a bit silly they become obsessed with them yet can't feed at all, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't look at me, I think it's silly that any Daeva would drink twice on purpose. But, people on the forum assured me that happens in their games, so, I'm guessing they somehow don't consider health levels of damage to be &quot;harm?&quot; Like, since the Kiss is nice, maybe they justify it as ok despite the literal harm being caused?<br /> <br /> Or Daeva just detach quickly? I don't know how people do it. My table just has Daeva that feed promiscuously and avoid the dependency thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  typo 03-20-2016, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T22:15:57-07:00","id":850032,"title":"","content":"Then how about having the curse activate when the gangrel character does an extended roll. (the curse could still be risk of frenzy or simply negative modifiers)<br /> That would mean that gangrel have a tendency to focus on action that have an immediate fulfillment iwhereas extended roll show a more advanced thought process more distanced from primal instinct. Thus we place an emphasis on a direct, crude and savage stereotype for the gangrel character.<br /> its not perfect but it could be closer to what you want ... i hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T22:26:31-07:00","id":850036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850032#post850032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then how about having the curse activate when the gangrel character does an extended roll. (the curse could still be risk of frenzy or simply negative modifiers)<br /> That would mean that gangrel have a tendency to focus on action that have an immediate fulfillment iwhereas extended roll show a more advanced thought process more distanced from primal instinct. Thus we place an emphasis on a direct, crude and savage stereotype for the gangrel character.<br /> its not perfect but it could be closer to what you want ... i hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is definitely closer. I like the idea, I really do, but I think I need to look through at what extended rolls are in the game. The one that immediately jumps out at me is running. I don't think they should be penalized for chases. Or climbing. I'm not even totally sure I want them to be penalized to, say, fix up their motorcycle, since that might be their outlet for running wild. It's certainly good thinking, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T06:28:50-07:00","id":850112,"title":"","content":"Nice thread and interesting points all around. And how about about giving a cumulative penalty each time a Gangrel succesfully avoids a Frenzy? This way, you could emphasize the need the Gangrel has to give into the Beast, and making the character to choose very carefully which battles against the inner monster needs to fight and which ones needs to let go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T06:36:55-07:00","id":850114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850112#post850112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice thread and interesting points all around. And how about about giving a cumulative penalty each time a Gangrel succesfully avoids a Frenzy? This way, you could emphasize the need the Gangrel has to give into the Beast, and making the character to choose very carefully which battles against the inner monster needs to fight and which ones needs to let go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And give them ability to reset the penalty to 0 with Willpower expenditure. &quot;Do I Willpower it immediately, or can I take it for little longer?&quot; Obviously, this works better in games where Willpower management is real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T07:05:00-07:00","id":850117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850114#post850114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And give them ability to reset the penalty to 0 with Willpower expenditure. &quot;Do I Willpower it immediately, or can I take it for little longer?&quot; Obviously, this works better in games where Willpower management is real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice touch! It would allow also to go for a harsher Beast if needed, negating one penalty point for one willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T07:08:14-07:00","id":850118,"title":"","content":"The Daeva curse write up mentions them either tending towards promiscuity or cultivating &quot;massive harems and herds&quot; which indicates that feeding from a mortal you're pseudo-bonded to isn't an issue. That aside the bond requires a failed humanity roll to establish, so you could potentially feed from the same mortal all you like and never get Dependent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T08:41:15-07:00","id":850136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850112#post850112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice thread and interesting points all around. And how about about giving a cumulative penalty each time a Gangrel succesfully avoids a Frenzy? This way, you could emphasize the need the Gangrel has to give into the Beast, and making the character to choose very carefully which battles against the inner monster needs to fight and which ones needs to let go. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually already a rule. It's called the Tempted condition, and you get it when you succeed (without exceptionally succeeding) on any Frenzy roll.<br /> <br /> But, again, I really don't want Frenzy to be the ultimate result. I want them to act bestial <i>without</i> necessarily being forced to Frenzy. Frenzy sucks--it's not fun for the player, it's awful to lose control. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850114#post850114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And give them ability to reset the penalty to 0 with Willpower expenditure. &quot;Do I Willpower it immediately, or can I take it for little longer?&quot; Obviously, this works better in games where Willpower management is real.</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower management in my game is pretty harsh, actually. Without anchors, you don't basically always have full Willpower. You have to actually conserve it, because you mostly just get it back 1/day. There are a few other circumstances where they regain it--awesome triumphs and victories, for example, but yeah, it's tough, instead of, &quot;Yeah, you pretty much always have +3 to everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850118#post850118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva curse write up mentions them either tending towards promiscuity or cultivating &quot;massive harems and herds&quot; which indicates that feeding from a mortal you're pseudo-bonded to isn't an issue. That aside the bond requires a failed humanity roll to establish, so you could potentially feed from the same mortal all you like and never get Dependent.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true, you can avoid Dependency. But I can't imagine why you'd risk it. That said, the write up says &quot;massive harems and herds.&quot; It doesn't say that they also don't face constant Humanity 3 breaking points. Or, maybe, if your herd is large enough, you can minimize how often you have to drink from the same person, reducing the chances of the Dependency? I don't know, it never seems worth risking, though. Cultivate feeding grounds in a tourist area instead of a herd--it's safer.<br /> <br /> But, look, I'm not here to police people's games. If other GMs want to rule that dealing health boxes of damage to someone isn't &quot;harm&quot; because it feels good or whatever, they can do that. No big deal. But at my table, I wouldn't feed from the same guy twice as a Daeva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T10:47:02-07:00","id":850186,"title":"","content":"I think this is pretty clearly one of those cases where you have to remember that Breaking Points are guidelines, not absolute lists, and are meant to be edited and manipulated on the fly.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I'm not sure I buy the concept that 'harm' equates purely to health levels. Would I force a level 3 sin for a Daeva with a BDSM herd every time they get little deep? Would I force the same for consensual or 'soft' feeding scenes? No to both. I can think of other cases, too. A bonded Childe-to-sire pair in the Circle who engage in blood rituals w/ blades or implements? Not gonna force a check when they are doing their Cruac stuff together. Ghoul gets shot with an arrow, Daeva has to push the arrow out causing more pain/damage so the wound can be cleaned and disinfected. Not gonna force a check. I don't think Kindred face a Level 3 check every time they bite their Regnant to be fed again, for that matter.<br /> <br /> But I <i>would </i>force a check for the creepy Daeva who takes by force just a single drop of blood from their obsessee, even if they never technically cause a full health level of damage.<br /> <br /> Once again, Breaking Points are very much one of those story-mechanics that you prefer not to use. It's meant to be enforced only when <i>dramatically </i>important to the <i>narrative</i>. If you are going to convert it to an exhaustive list of checks that should occur every time they happen regardless of circumstances, I really don't think you do that correctly by just porting everything over and saying that equals true simulation. There are things missing on that list, and things that shouldn't trigger every time.<br /> <br /> I would not recommend porting over a rule that forces Daeva to make a breaking point every time they feed on an obsessee. But in a world where that rule is in place, of course it doesn't make any sense for Deava to risk obsession if they have any care at all for their Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","user":"Holy","date":".  typos 03-20-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T11:45:42-07:00","id":850211,"title":"","content":"On a condition - my (still Vampire-uninformed) ballpark would be something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Cornered Beast</b><br /> You feel trapped and feel an urge to break through the fetters placed on you, whether metaphorical or literal. You take a -2 penalty to all actions that aren't directly intended to breach the restrictions placed on you - breaking or unlocking the door of a prison cell or flouting rules of etiquette and politeness would not be penalised, for example, but talking to the inhabitants of the other cells (except to order them to help you escape) likely would.<br /> Resolution: Escape the fetters, at least for the immediate future. This might mean breaking out of a locked room and escaping the alerted guards, or finding solitude after a formal social event's rules of etiquette became too much for you.<br /> <br /> I don't know enough about Clan banes to judge when the Condition should be gained, but this is my first stab at throwing something together that encourages the sort of direct approach you were looking for - some of the ideas on the previous page may feed in to get the right feel. It's likely to boil down to &quot;if you act too reserved, indirect and polite, your Beast gets restless and you start getting <i>quite bad</i> at doing that until you flip out and leave.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T18:25:51-07:00","id":850352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850211#post850211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a condition - my (still Vampire-uninformed) ballpark would be something like:<br /> <br /> <b>Cornered Beast</b><br /> You feel trapped and feel an urge to break through the fetters placed on you, whether metaphorical or literal. You take a -2 penalty to all actions that aren't directly intended to breach the restrictions placed on you - breaking or unlocking the door of a prison cell or flouting rules of etiquette and politeness would not be penalised, for example, but talking to the inhabitants of the other cells (except to order them to help you escape) likely would.<br /> Resolution: Escape the fetters, at least for the immediate future. This might mean breaking out of a locked room and escaping the alerted guards, or finding solitude after a formal social event's rules of etiquette became too much for you.<br /> <br /> I don't know enough about Clan banes to judge when the Condition should be gained, but this is my first stab at throwing something together that encourages the sort of direct approach you were looking for - some of the ideas on the previous page may feed in to get the right feel. It's likely to boil down to &quot;if you act too reserved, indirect and polite, your Beast gets restless and you start getting <i>quite bad</i> at doing that until you flip out and leave.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a good start. I like it. I will work on refining it, too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T00:07:21-07:00","id":850443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850118#post850118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Daeva curse write up mentions them either tending towards promiscuity or cultivating &quot;massive harems and herds&quot; which indicates that feeding from a mortal you're pseudo-bonded to isn't an issue. That aside the bond requires a failed humanity roll to establish, so you could potentially feed from the same mortal all you like and never get Dependent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ruled that as long the Daeva is feeding non-forcefully from a healthy person and taking only 1 Vitae (or 2, or 3, from mortals with high Stamina), it doesn't count.<br /> After all your Ghoul isn't going to freak out because you're offering him the opportunity to drink from your wrist, isn't him? Same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T00:50:24-07:00","id":850447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850443#post850443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I ruled that as long the Daeva is feeding non-forcefully from a healthy person and taking only 1 Vitae (or 2, or 3, from mortals with high Stamina), it doesn't count.<br /> After all your Ghoul isn't going to freak out because you're offering him the opportunity to drink from your wrist, isn't him? Same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much been how I handle it as well. As long as you're using the Kiss, don't take so much that you cause the Drained Condition, and don't fill up their rightmost hit boxes it doesn't count as harm, at least as far as the Daeva clan bane is concerned. So a Daeva still has to have a pretty sizable herd, simply because it takes a while for people to replenish that much blood (heal lethal), but the Daeva don't have to take a shotgun to their Humanity just to do what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 03-21-2016, 03:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T02:47:41-07:00","id":850465,"title":"","content":"I'd try and keep it easy, but still related to the frenzy.<br /> If you successfully resist a frenzy, lose 1 Willpower.<br /> There, done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:27:19-07:00","id":850659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850443#post850443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ruled that as long the Daeva is feeding non-forcefully from a healthy person and taking only 1 Vitae (or 2, or 3, from mortals with high Stamina), it doesn't count.<br /> After all your Ghoul isn't going to freak out because you're offering him the opportunity to drink from your wrist, isn't him? Same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, other people can do it as they like. To me, though, it's not the same thing, because vampires take no harm, no lethal damage, from giving blood to someone, nor do they take lethal damage from various ways to release that blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850465#post850465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd try and keep it easy, but still related to the frenzy.<br /> If you successfully resist a frenzy, lose 1 Willpower.<br /> There, done.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad that works for you, but I'm trying to avoid encouraging frenzy. Frenzy isn't a fun game mechanic, at least not for me or any person I play with. It's a loss condition. It's &quot;you done fucked up, now you lose control!&quot; It's bad. Riding the Wave is using this obviously bad thing for a little bit of good, but, no, frenzying sucks. I have a couple of players, actually, who wish it wasn't even in the game at all (though, no, I and the rest of us like it and explained to them that it's totally avoidable for the most part, short of supernatural powers). <br /> <br /> So, the idea that the Gangrel just have to frenzy a lot is not satisfying to me. It's especially problematic because my city is run by a Gangrel Bloodline, and, while they have the hint of the wild about them, they are not rampaging lunatics. It doesn't fit. <br /> <br /> I really want to play with this idea of Confinement and the Cornered Beast suggestion above. It's extra ironic because the city's founder became a vampire/his own bloodline as a result of a deal made with a true fae. For them to become a vampire bloodline that hates being bound to have been created via binding contract is very intriguing to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T10:37:35-07:00","id":850664,"title":"","content":"Then why not remove the Beast, altogether? There's a system floating around in this forum which replaces it with the Hunger. Check it out, it might be more to your liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:36:33-07:00","id":850710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850664#post850664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why not remove the Beast, altogether? There's a system floating around in this forum which replaces it with the Hunger. Check it out, it might be more to your liking.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I want to remove the Beast. Most of us like it being there. Just because frenzying isn't fun, because it's a loss condition, doesn't mean I don't want it there. That said, I am intrigued enough that I've been looking to find it. I tried the forum search and the google search, but came up with nothing useful. Most of the google searches came up with Beast: the Primordial posts, since there's apparently a Hunger mechanic in there.<br /> <br /> Do you, by chance, know where this system is? Do you have a link?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T11:44:50-07:00","id":850720,"title":"","content":"It seems it isn't completely fleshed out, but this should get you started:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/837964-how-do-you-hack-your-setting?p=838629#post838629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While working on that, I realized, watching some related media, that I was never very fond of &quot;The Beast&quot;. So I replaced it with &quot;The Hunger.&quot; Instead of having to constantly worry about frenzy and rotshreck, a vampire instead has to make an effort of will to pull off a victim when feeding. They also gain a new stated called &quot;Hungry&quot;if their Blood Pool is less than half full. Normally, in my games, vamps all have Blush of life when sated, and when they get Hungry, they start to degrade.At Hungry, they look like classic WoD vamps, pale, cold to the touch, no pulse. At 1/4 or less, they gain &quot;Starving&quot;, and start to look more like Cappadocians. Each state has penalties to the Hunger checks when feeding. A botch means they go on a feeding rampage.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T19:11:34-07:00","id":850921,"title":"","content":"Ok, no, I still like the Beast. That Hunger thing is for a different kind of vampire, and it still involves Frenzy, which is the thing I'd be tempted to remove anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T01:00:17-07:00","id":851014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=850136#post850136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's true, you can avoid Dependency. But I can't imagine why you'd risk it. That said, the write up says &quot;massive harems and herds.&quot; It doesn't say that they also don't face constant Humanity 3 breaking points.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rule book doesn't say that, but the FAQ does.<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Feeding, in of itself, doesn't count as harming the target of Daeva's Dependent Condition. You're free to run it differently of course, but I think the chance of a lifetime bond to the mortal is risk enough.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T05:52:33-07:00","id":851094,"title":"","content":"Why do you consider frenzying a loss condition?<br /> EDIT<br /> To elaborate, I can see oWoD Frenzy as a loss condition (i didn't really care enough for 1st ed Requiem to remember it's rules), but in 2nd ed, you as a player are still in control of your character by default, you get a power boost, and most importantly, apparently you still get benefits of the Frenzy while spending willpower points to ride it, without the drawbacks.<br /> EDIT 2<br /> Penalize Gangrel's ability to resist frenzy, but make sure that their ability to Ride the Wave is untouched and better choice due to being non penalized, so Gangrels start Riding the Wave more often and thus create a gameplay pattern you are looking for?<br /> EDIT 3<br /> While book is unclear on it, and I didn't consider it being a thing while reading it, one of devs here said that attempting to Ride the Wave is already giving you the benefits of the frenzy; you get the full package while trying to accumulate 5 successes. Apparently that's the desired state of rules, and it changed my perception of frenzying and riding the wave dramatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-22-2016, 09:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T09:03:25-07:00","id":851173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851094#post851094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you consider frenzying a loss condition?<br /> EDIT<br /> To elaborate, I can see oWoD Frenzy as a loss condition (i didn't really care enough for 1st ed Requiem to remember it's rules), but in 2nd ed, you as a player are still in control of your character by default, you get a power boost, and most importantly, apparently you still get benefits of the Frenzy while spending willpower points to ride it, without the drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of that changed from 1e or even the classic WoD. You always controlled your character (sort of...your character is out of control and you just get to say the things they're forced to do). You get a power boost in all editions, and it's actually a weaker boost in 2e for starting characters.<br /> <br /> Hmm, riding the wave is really different than I remember, now that I'm re-reading it. Was there a change between Blood and Smoke and Requiem 2e? I could have sworn there was a coil specifically that let you ride the wave instead of involuntarily frenzying, but now, it seems like riding the wave is a default thing you can do while involuntarily frenzying. That's...really weird. That certainly helps frenzying be less awful, but you character is still out of control. You're just barely directing them.<br /> <br /> And it's a loss condition because frenzies are 90% avoidable. Unless someone is using powers like Animalism 4 on you, or someone is particularly cruel for basically no reason and tries to humiliate you just for fun, frenzies are totally within your grasp to stop. You can just not get hungry. Major source of frenzy closed. Avoid fire and sunlight--again, duh. Don't let your friends/lovers get hurt. Don't cause waves such that people target you for mockery and humiliation. Don't screw up so that your superior insults you. Don't screw up so badly that your inferior does. And when all else fails, roll Resolve + Composure, so, you know, have a bunch of dice in that pool. The sources of provocation are mostly in your hands--so when you frenzy, it's because you blew it.<br /> <br /> The whole purpose of frenzy is that it's a bad thing, Thematically, it's the reminder of what happens when you screw up, it's the beast rising to the surface when one of the goals of the game is to suppress the beast and hang on to your humanity. Losing humanity, giving in to the beast, is losing yourself, losing you. Of course a manifestation of that is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851094#post851094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT 2<br /> Penalize Gangrel's ability to resist frenzy, but make sure that their ability to Ride the Wave is untouched and better choice due to being non penalized, so Gangrels start Riding the Wave more often and thus create a gameplay pattern you are looking for?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a better gameplay pattern than the current one, but it's not what I really want. I don't want to force anyone to frenzy, though, in an ideal circumstance. I'd like to keep it a bad thing. I'd like for the Gangrel to be wild without embracing the Beast. Like, their wildness keeps the Beast in check as much as someone else's stoicism.<br /> <br /> Hmm, maybe I can do something with forcing them to Lash Out, rather than forcing them to frenzy more?<br /> <br /> Maybe the Kerberos flaw could work as a general Gangrel flaw? I don't know if I only like it in theory, though. I wonder if it might get annoying to have every Gangrel lashing out constantly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 03-22-2016, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T02:24:28-07:00","id":851636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851173#post851173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of that changed from 1e or even the classic WoD. You always controlled your character (sort of...your character is out of control and you just get to say the things they're forced to do). You get a power boost in all editions, and it's actually a weaker boost in 2e for starting characters.<br /> <br /> Hmm, riding the wave is really different than I remember, now that I'm re-reading it. Was there a change between Blood and Smoke and Requiem 2e? I could have sworn there was a coil specifically that let you ride the wave instead of involuntarily frenzying, but now,<b> it seems like riding the wave is a default thing you can do while involuntarily frenzying.</b> That's...really weird. That certainly helps frenzying be less awful, but you character is still out of control. You're just barely directing them.<br /> <br /> And it's a loss condition because frenzies are 90% avoidable. Unless someone is using powers like Animalism 4 on you, or someone is particularly cruel for basically no reason and tries to humiliate you just for fun, frenzies are totally within your grasp to stop. You can just not get hungry. Major source of frenzy closed. Avoid fire and sunlight--again, duh. Don't let your friends/lovers get hurt. Don't cause waves such that people target you for mockery and humiliation. Don't screw up so that your superior insults you. Don't screw up so badly that your inferior does. And when all else fails, roll Resolve + Composure, so, you know, have a bunch of dice in that pool. The sources of provocation are mostly in your hands--so when you frenzy, it's because you blew it.<br /> <br /> The whole purpose of frenzy is that it's a bad thing, Thematically, it's the reminder of what happens when you screw up, it's the beast rising to the surface when one of the goals of the game is to suppress the beast and hang on to your humanity. Losing humanity, giving in to the beast, is losing yourself, losing you. Of course a manifestation of that is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> That's a better gameplay pattern than the current one, but it's not what I really want. I don't want to force anyone to frenzy, though, in an ideal circumstance. I'd like to keep it a bad thing. I'd like for the Gangrel to be wild without embracing the Beast. Like, their wildness keeps the Beast in check as much as someone else's stoicism.<br /> <br /> Hmm, maybe I can do something with forcing them to Lash Out, rather than forcing them to frenzy more?<br /> <br /> Maybe the Kerberos flaw could work as a general Gangrel flaw? I don't know if I only like it in theory, though. I wonder if it might get annoying to have every Gangrel lashing out constantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bolded part is not true. If you're rolling for involuntary frenzy - you don't get to ride the wave. Only if you anticipate involuntary frenzy and pre-empt it with a Ride the Wave. <br /> The Coil still exists. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T06:39:27-07:00","id":851709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851636#post851636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bolded part is not true. If you're rolling for involuntary frenzy - you don't get to ride the wave. Only if you anticipate involuntary frenzy and pre-empt it with a Ride the Wave.<br /> The Coil still exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>While the coil still exists, I think, re-reading everything, that the intention of Wyrm 1 is that it basically lets you skip the Riding the Wave rolls--just spend a single willpower and you're done. Having played classic WoD and Requiem 1st, I assumed Riding the Wave was a thing you chose to do when you were not otherwise frenzying, and that it took actions to attempt. But rereading just 2e, it seems like Riding the Wave is an option you can take instead of resisting an involuntary frenzy. It's not written very clearly, that's for sure, but this line, especially, seals it for me: &quot;This desire does not have to align with the provocation. For example, if Victoria risks frenzy because she\u2019s starved, she might choose to kill Dominic instead of feeding.&quot; You couldn't have a provocation unless you were faced with an involuntary frenzy in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T07:35:59-07:00","id":851736,"title":"","content":"Have to agree with The Storyteller on this one. When provoked, you have three options:<ul><li><i>Relinquish</i>. Immediately enter frenzy with the target/agenda of the beast set by the provocation.</li> <li><i>Resist</i>. Roll Resolve + Composure with modifiers per sidebar p104. On a failure, enter frenzy with the target/agenda of the beast set by the provocation.</li> <li><i>Ride</i>. Extended Action, Cost 1 WP per Roll. &quot;Normal&quot; Resolve + Composure roll (I interpret this to mean the modifiers from p104 still apply). Target = 5 Successes. Failure, or running out of Willpower enters a normal frenzy with the target/agenda of the beast set by the provocation. Success allows the player to set the target/agenda of the beast.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T07:43:15-07:00","id":851742,"title":"","content":"That's an interpretation, for sure. But I don't think that it's RAW or even RAI. <br /> For example, defending against frenzy section speaks nothing about this. all it says is &quot;WP delays your roll&quot;. There would be very little point to delay your roll if you could roll for a different objective. (Barring super small dice pools).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:11:31-07:00","id":851757,"title":"","content":"So, I agree that it feels weird that you can delay your roll at the same price as riding the wave. That's what initially threw me off. I thought exactly as you until yesterday when comments here prompted me to re-read everything. I think they wanted to make Ride the Wave way more attractive and common. Resisting with willpower might be purposefully worse to encourage riding waves. The only reason I could think of to delay is to have a chance to escape or remove the provocation, rendering the roll moot at the end. For example, when hunger frenzying, run away from the victim and lock yourself in a room or something. Even if you still roll, you at least no longer suffer the penalties to being near blood.<br /> <br /> Regardless, here's my first draft. Thank you to those who've helped give me ideas, so far. What do you think now? How can I refine it? Is it out of theme? Is it too vague? Etc., etc.?<br /> <br /> Gangrel: The Feral Curse<br /> Gangrel must run wild and free; they cannot abide confinement, be it physical or metaphorical. Entering a contract or swearing an Oath is one thing--one enters such an agreement of their own free will--but when othewise forced into a corner, Gangrel chafe and lash out, gaining the Cornered Beast condition. Consider a Gangrel &quot;confined&quot; when they are in a situation, against their will, in which simply walking away is not an option. This applies equally to social obligations and politcal traps as physical retraints. The rules of Elysium do not normally trigger this bane, but other, more one sided rules and regulations certainly might. <br /> <br /> Cornered Beast<br /> You feel trapped and must escape at all costs. The closer your Beast lies to the surface, the worse this feeling becomes, as the devil inside seethes with resentment at your confinement. You must take direct action, either to escape the situation or to lash out at your perceived captors. All other non-reflexive actions require a willpower point to attempt and are capped by your Humanity. Rolls to resist frenzy suffer a penalty equal to the penalty you suffer on social rolls relating to humans due to low Humanity. <br /> Possible Sources: The Gangrel clan bane<br /> Resolution: Frenzy or escape the confinement that triggered this condition<br /> Beat: n/a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:20:58-07:00","id":851761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851757#post851757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I agree that it feels weird that you can delay your roll at the same price as riding the wave. That's what initially threw me off. I thought exactly as you until yesterday when comments here prompted me to re-read everything. I think they wanted to make Ride the Wave way more attractive and common. Resisting with willpower might be purposefully worse to encourage riding waves. The only reason I could think of to delay is to have a chance to escape or remove the provocation, rendering the roll moot at the end. For example, when hunger frenzying, run away from the victim and lock yourself in a room or something. Even if you still roll, you at least no longer suffer the penalties to being near blood.<br /> <br /> Regardless, here's my first draft. Thank you to those who've helped give me ideas, so far. What do you think now? How can I refine it? Is it out of theme? Is it too vague? Etc., etc.?<br /> <br /> Gangrel: The Feral Curse<br /> Gangrel must run wild and free; they cannot abide confinement, be it physical or metaphorical. Entering a contract or swearing an Oath is one thing--one enters such an agreement of their own free will--but when othewise forced into a corner, Gangrel chafe and lash out, gaining the Cornered Beast condition. Consider a Gangrel &quot;confined&quot; when they are in a situation, against their will, in which simply walking away is not an option. This applies equally to social obligations and politcal traps as physical retraints. The rules of Elysium do not normally trigger this bane, but other, more one sided rules and regulations certainly might.<br /> <br /> Cornered Beast<br /> You feel trapped and must escape at all costs. The closer your Beast lies to the surface, the worse this feeling becomes, as the devil inside seethes with resentment at your confinement. You must take direct action, either to escape the situation or to lash out at your perceived captors. All other non-reflexive actions require a willpower point to attempt and are capped by your Humanity. Rolls to resist frenzy suffer a penalty equal to the penalty you suffer on social rolls relating to humans due to low Humanity.<br /> Possible Sources: The Gangrel clan bane<br /> Resolution: Frenzy or escape the confinement that triggered this condition<br /> Beat: n/a</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To me, this is just a reflavored Frenzy, with additional mechanics thrown in. <br /> <br /> What's wrong with instead of gaining the condition getting a Frenzy trigger? It's also direct action to escape/lash out ,with WP to delay it further (or if we follow your interpretation, ride the wave, which might as well be &quot;escape&quot;. Even further, this is a worse thing than a Frenzy since you also don't get the bonuses. And it also uses the dreadful &quot;capped by humanity rule&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T09:28:53-07:00","id":851823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851742#post851742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interpretation, for sure. But I don't think that it's RAW or even RAI.<br /> For example, defending against frenzy section speaks nothing about this. all it says is &quot;WP delays your roll&quot;. There would be very little point to delay your roll if you could roll for a different objective. (Barring super small dice pools).</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower 'delaying your roll' is referencing the extra rules for spending Willpower on Frenzy. Instead of the normal (+3) to a rolled pool, spending Willpower gives you a turn of freedom as you struggle against the Frenzy. As soon as you stop spending Willpower, you make the delayed roll with a (+1) bonus per Willpower spent.<br /> <br /> Note that Willpower is not required to be spent to resist frenzy. You can immediately roll Resolve + Composure + Modifiers to resist without delaying at all. The delay only happens if you want an additional bonus.<br /> <br /> The point of Resisting vs. Riding is that one <i>stops</i> the Frenzy, meaning you don't have to flee/fight/feed from a target at all. Also, there is only one success needed to resist, vs. 5 successes needed to Ride the Wave. Even with average Resolve + Composure pools (6 Dice), adding any sort of modifiers in there, like for hunger or wound penalties, and it's not uncommon to fail the Ride check on the extended roll. Finally, unless you get an Exceptional Success out of the gate, you're looking at a minimum of 2 WP spent to ride, as you pay the cost each roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T10:44:05-07:00","id":851861,"title":"","content":"I also wonder how the blood bond factor into this as its (sometimes) akin to being forced into a one sided social situation.<br /> Would it incur the condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T14:20:48-07:00","id":852011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851823#post851823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of Resisting vs. Riding is that one <i>stops</i> the Frenzy, meaning you don't have to flee/fight/feed from a target at all. Also, there is only one success needed to resist, vs. 5 successes needed to Ride the Wave. Even with average Resolve + Composure pools (6 Dice), adding any sort of modifiers in there, like for hunger or wound penalties, and it's not uncommon to fail the Ride check on the extended roll. Finally, unless you get an Exceptional Success out of the gate, you're looking at a minimum of 2 WP spent to ride, as you pay the cost each roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, the disconnect was just that, in previous versions, Riding the Wave was a thing you chose to do when you otherwise weren't going to frenzy. It let you purposefully frenzy when not called for. I see now, though, that Coil of the Wyrm 1 is now the only way to do that. It does make more thematic sense, this way, though. It will be strange getting used to it.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851761#post851761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, this is just a reflavored Frenzy, with additional mechanics thrown in.<br /> <br /> What's wrong with instead of gaining the condition getting a Frenzy trigger? It's also direct action to escape/lash out ,with WP to delay it further (or if we follow your interpretation, ride the wave, which might as well be &quot;escape&quot;. Even further, this is a worse thing than a Frenzy since you also don't get the bonuses.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, I need to figure out if this is a problem with the actual rules themselves, or my ability to convey them. I don't think it's a reflavored frenzy at all, nor do I think it's worse than frenzy. I think it's way better and more flexible. Here are a couple of circumstances and how they might play out under a &quot;you just frenzy&quot; version of the rules vs. what I thought I was writing:<br /> <br /> Scenario 1: You're at a club, at the far end of the bar, scoping out the scene. A man sidles up, resting one arm on the bar and the other on the wall, trapping you in the corner. &quot;Hey sweet heart,&quot; he says, &quot;can I buy you a drink?&quot;<br /> <br /> Frenzy: Nearly foaming at the mouth, you rip his throat out in front of a club full of people. Good luck with that Masquerade breach, Gangrel.<br /> As is, Option A: You spend a willpower and say, &quot;Sure, baby. (Insert drink here). You let him pick you up and get a meal out of it.<br /> Option B: You snarl, Lashing out with the Monstrous Beast, before snapping &quot;Fuck off, shitbag&quot; (and probably rolling Intimidate)<br /> Option C: You grab him closer, Lashing out with the Seductive Beast, before pushing him out to the dance floor. You're going to fuck him and feed tonight.<br /> <br /> Scenario 2: You just fed and dumped the body in an alley way. A group of thugs with weapons block the alley off and start edging closer. &quot;I just need to ask you a few questions. Answer them, and you're free to go, I swear.&quot;<br /> <br /> Frenzy: Nearly foaming at the mouth, you rip his throat out in front of everyone there. A fight ensues that causes you unnecessary damage/effective blood loss, and the scuffle draws even more attention from locals and law enforcement. Worse, what if one gets away to reveal what happened, and helpless bystanders come down the alley to see if you're ok? More dead. Good job, Gangrel.<br /> Option A: Spend a willpower and say, &quot;Ok, what do you want to know?&quot;<br /> Option B: Snarl/growl/roar and Lash Out with the Monstrous Beast against the leader and intimidate the crap out of him, so they back off. Or so they attack you and you can fight smart, rather than savagely, perhaps grabbing the leader and holding him at knife point or something so the gang backs down.<br /> Option C: Parkour up the wall and onto the roof of the building nearby and escape cleanly.<br /> Option D: Use animalism 3 or 4 to get away. Either swarms of rats or birds or something fills the alley, or they all go nuts on each other while you slip away. Either way, can't do that while frenzied.<br /> <br /> Scenario 3: You're in a cage that is too strong to just break out of normally.<br /> <br /> Frenzy: Foaming at the mouth, you slam against the cage over and over ad nauseam with no hope of actually even ending the frenzy and making it very unlikely anyone will let you out without putting you down first. Unless you have Claws of the Unholy, then this might be ok.<br /> Option A: Pick the lock with Larceny<br /> Option B: Sink into the floor under the cage, hope they move/open the cage to check on where you could possibly have gone; or turn into an animal small enough to fit through the bars, or just turn into mist.<br /> Option C: Scream, howl, yell, rant, and rave until someone comes to check on you, Lash out with the Competitive Beast, then use some willpower to challenge them to something where they'd have to let you out. Or the Seductive Beast and some willpower to try to see if they'll open the cage to bang you. Or Monstrous Beast and taunt them to fight you, so they have to open it to get you.<br /> Option D: Spend some willpower and wait. When someone comes by close to the cage, spend more willpower and pick their pockets for the keys<br /> Option E: If you have claws of the unholy and Wyrm 1, frenzy and destroy the cage--just because it's not forced on you doesn't mean it isn't a good idea some times. <br /> <br /> So, yeah, I feel like it forces action, yes, but doesn't limit you the same way frenzy does. I'm still open to your point of view on this...I certainly don't want to just give an alternate form of frenzy. Was I just unclear in writing it up the first time? If that was the issue, how can I fix that? If not, what was wrong? Is it just so distasteful that you'd still rather frenzy?<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851761#post851761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it also uses the dreadful &quot;capped by humanity rule&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So, I don't know why it's so dreaded or bad, but, that's readily fixable. I can just apply the same penalty as you get to social rolls from low Humanity instead. I just want to include Humanity somehow. Every single clan flaw interacts with Humanity in some way that make it less bad for you with higher Humanity<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=851861#post851861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also wonder how the blood bond factor into this as its (sometimes) akin to being forced into a one sided social situation.<br /> Would it incur the condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think that being threatened with blood bonding would get a Gangrel's hackles up in preparation/fear of confinement, but once it actually happens, you'd no longer feel trapped, you'd like it. The same would apply for mind control powers. While you are under the effects, you wouldn't feel confined, you'd feel fine with it. But you'd be pissed later. And before, if you saw it coming.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T23:22:24-07:00","id":852261,"title":"","content":"1. I don't think any of those scenarios would cause Frenzy, and if they did it would be with no penalty to the roll or very minimal.<br /> <br /> 2. When you Frenzy, your ST sets the goal for the Frenzy. It isn't a &quot;kill whoever is closest to you&quot; sort of thing. It's a &quot;achieve your goal in the most direct way possible&quot; sort of thing. For secenario two, for example, the frenzy goal could be &quot;get the hell out of here&quot; and you just run away after bowling over the guys between you and the exit. If you Ride the Wave, you can set your own goal even.<br /> <br /> It's fight or flight, not just fight. That's why flames trigger it, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:41:25-07:00","id":852333,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's because I started my nwod Vampire adventure with 2nd ed, but from reading the book, ive got an impression that frenzy is a dangerous thing, but often actually a tool you can use to get an advantage. I guess thats because we never really defaultet frenzy to Hulk Smash!. Like, in a lot of your examples of &quot;provoke them to embarass then&quot;, frenzy responses wouldn't mean necessarily &quot;grab him by the throat screaming&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:58:02-07:00","id":852336,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the Beast isn't stupid, you don't just rip out every throat that comes within range, you're entirely capable of just punching someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T05:13:33-07:00","id":852341,"title":"","content":"A valid goal in most of those situations is &quot;Get this asshole away&quot; (since he's in your personal space/cornering you), the Beast doesn't have to murder him immediately. Just a punch and a spit at his face is enough to get the point across. And if he pushes for - well next frenzy might not be so lucky, but it's not immediately &quot;let's murderhobo everybody around&quot;. It has an objective, and it's deliberately no longer just &quot;fight or flight&quot;, it's what you want/need the most with &quot;fuck the consequences&quot;. <br /> <br /> Fuck the consequences does not mean &quot;murder everybody&quot;. It just means that you'll get what you want (like making sure this guy never comes to you again).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T06:26:51-07:00","id":852371,"title":"","content":"Maybe encourage Gangrel to <i>act</i> like they're in a frenzy, without actually putting them there? The new Frenzy paradigm is &quot;get what you want <i>right now</i> in the most direct way possible,&quot; so encourage Gangrel players to do that? Maybe something like &quot;in a situation in which the <i>immediate</i> goal has two or more paths to achieve it, Gangrel suffer a penalty to all but the most direct one.&quot; For example, they need to get past a locked a door. They can pick the lock, climb up to the roof and open the skylight, or kick the door down. They suffer a penalty to picking the lock and climbing to the roof. The same would apply in a situation where a Gangrel is waiting on someone else to achieve the goal less directly. Rolling to keep their patience while a teammate picks the lock or sneaks in to unlock the door, failure meaning the Gangrel loses their patience and just breaks in.<br /> <br /> That having been said, I somewhat disagree with the idea that Gangrel &quot;primal behavior&quot; equates with &quot;instant gratification.&quot; Predators in the wild can be very cunning and forward-thinking. A wolf pack hunting an animal doesn't chase it, if the prey gets a chance to run you've already lost, burning more calories hunting it than you'll get from eating it. Rather, I'd penalize Gangrel for not pursuing their immediate goals. &quot;Immediate&quot; being a more flexible term here than above. If a Gangrel leaves his Haven with the intent of getting some Vitae, getting sidetracked from that goal should be a penalty. They're on the hunt, feeding is their goal, and someone popping up and saying &quot;hey, while I have you here, can I ask you a favor?&quot; is not going to get a warm response. Depending on the Gangrel in question, it could be &quot;I'm sorry, I'm in the middle of something right now, but I'll find you later and we can talk&quot; to &quot;Get the fuck out of my way before I pull out your ribcage and wear it as a hat.&quot; Once they've fed, they have a new goal: find the guy who wanted to ask them a favor. And anything getting in the way of that is also going to be trouble.<br /> <br /> Encourages players to step into the mindset of their characters, thinking &quot;what do I want right now, in this scene,&quot; and actively work towards it. The penalties could be mounting to certain kinds of rolls while being waylaid from their objective, making it harder for them to talk their way out of a hindering situation, until they either Frenzy from having their objective delayed (or possibly rendered impossible), or directly remove the obstacle, either by physical force or judicious use of Disciplines. The main penalties would be to social or mental rolls, I'd think. Basically, the Gangrel gets increasingly impatient and flustered by this interruption until they do something decisive about it. Of course, nothing prevents them from rolling really well immediately, with little or no penalty, extricating themselves from the distraction with minimal impact. But nothing prevents them from getting increasingly annoyed and inarticulate with the cop who just pulled them over for reckless driving, until their options for getting out of the situation all become equally unattractive. . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T07:25:04-07:00","id":852414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852261#post852261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. I don't think any of those scenarios would cause Frenzy, and if they did it would be with no penalty to the roll or very minimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it wouldn't. But they would make you feel confined, which would trigger my suggested Gangrel bane. It was suggested to me that my bane caused a pseudo frenzy and it would be better to just have them frenzy instead, so, I gave several examples as to why that's not the case. I like hyperbole as a rhetorical device, but I don't think it's super far off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852261#post852261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. When you Frenzy, your ST sets the goal for the Frenzy. It isn't a &quot;kill whoever is closest to you&quot; sort of thing. It's a &quot;achieve your goal in the most direct way possible&quot; sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852333#post852333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's because I started my nwod Vampire adventure with 2nd ed, but from reading the book, ive got an impression that frenzy is a dangerous thing, but often actually a tool you can use to get an advantage. I guess thats because we never really defaultet frenzy to Hulk Smash!. Like, in a lot of your examples of &quot;provoke them to embarass then&quot;, frenzy responses wouldn't mean necessarily &quot;grab him by the throat screaming&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852336#post852336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the Beast isn't stupid, you don't just rip out every throat that comes within range, you're entirely capable of just punching someone.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852341#post852341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A valid goal in most of those situations is &quot;Get this asshole away&quot; (since he's in your personal space/cornering you), the Beast doesn't have to murder him immediately. Just a punch and a spit at his face is enough to get the point across.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852341#post852341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has an objective, and it's deliberately no longer just &quot;fight or flight&quot;, it's what you want/need the most with &quot;fuck the consequences&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you guys suggesting this is a dramatically different frenzy paradigm than both Masquerade and 1e? Because when you anger frenzied in the past, you basically killed until all the bodies hit the floor. I guess I need to re-read again? Because when I hear &quot;frenzy,&quot; I don't think punching and pushing, I think all out fucking war with every deadly thing at your disposal. <br /> <br /> Grumble...why do they keep changing things? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm going to re-read and re-evaluate frenzy. This is bizarre.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852261#post852261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fight or flight, not just fight. That's why flames trigger it, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't think those scenarios, except maybe the cage, were scary so much as maddening. Fear frenzy seemed inappropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852371#post852371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe encourage Gangrel to <i>act</i> like they're in a frenzy, without actually putting them there? The new Frenzy paradigm is &quot;get what you want <i>right now</i> in the most direct way possible,&quot; so encourage Gangrel players to do that? Maybe something like &quot;in a situation in which the <i>immediate</i> goal has two or more paths to achieve it, Gangrel suffer a penalty to all but the most direct one.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't describe the state as &quot;acting like frenzied,&quot; didn't my suggestion basically do what you're saying? You have to act directly to escape the situation or lash out at those that you perceive as having confined you, or else you spend willpower and suffer a penalty.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852371#post852371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That having been said, I somewhat disagree with the idea that Gangrel &quot;primal behavior&quot; equates with &quot;instant gratification.&quot; Predators in the wild can be very cunning and forward-thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is part of why I didn't like the base &quot;you just frenzy a lot&quot; curse, and why I didn't go for &quot;you're impatient and can't do extended tasks&quot; either. Animals can wait. I know. That's why I went with &quot;they don't like being confined.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852371#post852371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, the Gangrel gets increasingly impatient and flustered by this interruption until they do something decisive about it. Of course, nothing prevents them from rolling really well immediately, with little or no penalty, extricating themselves from the distraction with minimal impact. But nothing prevents them from getting increasingly annoyed and inarticulate with the cop who just pulled them over for reckless driving, until their options for getting out of the situation all become equally unattractive. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>That pretty much goes against my clan bane paradigm, though. I want the flaw to be avoided, not embraced. I don't want it to come up much at all. I want there to be a way for the Gangrel to mostly avoid their flaw by acting in a certain, stereotypical-for-the-clan way. In this case, Gangrel would prefer out doorsy areas, with less corners to be backed in. They'd avoid fancy, formal affairs with suffocating rules. They'd avoid sitting in the corner, being always aware of exit points. They'd hunt on the rooftops instead of alleyways and haven in the dirt outside, rather than in elaborate labyrinthian underground complexes. You know, that kind of stuff.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T08:09:25-07:00","id":852439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852414#post852414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I wouldn't describe the state as &quot;acting like frenzied,&quot; didn't my suggestion basically do what you're saying? You have to act directly to escape the situation or lash out at those that you perceive as having confined you, or else you spend willpower and suffer a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was more about being direct in all actions, not just when under the conditions of &quot;being confined,&quot; which I think you yourself stated might have some trick definitions for the players to grasp (if not, I apologize for misreading.) Instead, the idea is to act in the most straightforward manner at all times. Don't like the way someone is behaving? You don't snicker at them and talk behind their back, you walk up to them and say &quot;I don't like your attitude, change it or I change it for you.&quot; Want blood? You don't play the dating game, you grab them or drug them or Dominate them. Don't like the Prince's latest decree? You don't lobby and debate and try to convince him to change his mind with rational discourse, you find a bunch of others who don't like it and tell the Prince to change his mind or deal with you and your friends.<br /> <br /> Granted, &quot;most direct method&quot; can also be somewhat nebulous, but it was the best I had at the time.<br /> <br /> As far as frenzy itself, even in Masquerade it wasn't &quot;kill until there's nothing left to kill.&quot; The only thing even close to that I remember is &quot;if blood is available, the vampire will drink until they're full.&quot; Which could kill one person or shitloads of people, depending on the vampire's Generation and how much blood they actually had. Other than that, exactly what a frenzy was remained pretty nebulous, and I think Requiem has been trying to hone in on what a Frenzy means more and more though 1st and 2nd Edition. I do recall reading the thing about the Beast having a goal in a Frenzy, and pursuing that goal to the exclusion of all others. A vampire frenzied by fire wants to get away from it, it's not going to attack anyone unless they try and prevent it from escaping, and then the attack is only so they can continue to flee. Whether they just shove someone aside or literally go through them depends on the individual vampire and what they have at their disposal. A vampire humiliated by a rival may certainly have as their goal &quot;kill that asshole,&quot; but they won't indiscriminately kill everyone else. Just their target and anyone who tries to get in their way. Less like sharks in a feeding frenzy, more like The Terminator. A goal pursued with single-minded purpose. At least, from my admittedly half-remembered reading way too long ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852414#post852414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That pretty much goes against my clan bane paradigm, though. I want the flaw to be avoided, not embraced. I don't want it to come up much at all. I want there to be a way for the Gangrel to mostly avoid their flaw by acting in a certain, stereotypical-for-the-clan way. In this case, Gangrel would prefer out doorsy areas, with less corners to be backed in. They'd avoid fancy, formal affairs with suffocating rules. They'd avoid sitting in the corner, being always aware of exit points. They'd hunt on the rooftops instead of alleyways and haven in the dirt outside, rather than in elaborate labyrinthian underground complexes. You know, that kind of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Forgive me, I get the Gangrel from Masquerade, 1E, and 2E all muddled in my head (they are pretty much my favorite Clan, though), so I wasn't quite sure which of the various Gangrel stereotypes you were aiming at. The problem I see with this is that &quot;avoiding fancy, formal affairs with suffocating rules&quot; basically means &quot;avoiding vampire society entirely,&quot; since vampires do love themselves lots of fancy formal affairs with suffocating rules. It also essentially bars Gangrel from three or four of the five Covenants (depending on exactly how formal and suffocating you think the rules of the Ordo Dracul, Invictus, Circle, and Sanctum are.) Perhaps a penalty based on how they approach the parts of the lives that are fully under their control? Joining a Covenant (or being part of Kindred society, or <i>any</i> society for that matter, inherently means giving up some personal freedoms to the greater whole). A Gangrel who's signed on to the Invictus knows exactly what they're getting themselves into, and so has no problem with the rules and etiquette of that group, because something about that must have appealed to them on some level to join. Rather, when they're &quot;on their own time,&quot; Gangrel have certain ways of doing things that apply a penalty when not done. Could be as simple as &quot;must keep a Haven in an outdoorsy area&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> The problem is that the Gangrel kind of embrace a pretty wide stereotype, so honing in on what, exactly, the Clan means is likely going to be different for everyone who reads them. &quot;Primal, animalistic vampire&quot; is far broader than &quot;Aristocratic power-hungry vampire&quot; or &quot;modern sexy vampire&quot; in a lot of ways. Maybe that's the stereotype that should be embraced. &quot;Primal animalism&quot; has a lot of different connotations, so maybe an array of Banes that the player picks one of, to reflect how the primal, animalistic nature of the Clan manifests in her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T09:58:18-07:00","id":852461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852414#post852414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you guys suggesting this is a dramatically different frenzy paradigm than both Masquerade and 1e? Because when you anger frenzied in the past, you basically killed until all the bodies hit the floor. I guess I need to re-read again? Because when I hear &quot;frenzy,&quot; I don't think punching and pushing, I think all out fucking war with every deadly thing at your disposal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was paraphrasing from the book.<br /> <br /> 'While frnezied, the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast's desires. She does so with immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon. If there's someone in the way, she throws him or decks him. If she's hungry, she bites the closest thing to her mouth. That said, the Beast isn't stupid. It's capable of doing the kind of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the predatory aura if that will help sate it.'<br /> <br /> Killing everything around you is more the domain of werewolf's Death Rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T12:06:03-07:00","id":852529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852439#post852439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> A vampire humiliated by a rival may certainly have as their goal &quot;kill that asshole,&quot; but they won't indiscriminately kill everyone else. Just their target and anyone who tries to get in their way. Less like sharks in a feeding frenzy, more like The Terminator. A goal pursued with single-minded purpose. At least, from my admittedly half-remembered reading way too long ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so it seems like most of the objection is scenario 2. I guess that did end up more like a Death Rage than a frenzy in my hyperbolic description. That said, if the frenzy goal was &quot;clear a path out of the alley,&quot; and bystanders walked into the alley, well, you'd have to clear them, too. But I can understand why that might not have been the goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852439#post852439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, I see. Forgive me, I get the Gangrel from Masquerade, 1E, and 2E all muddled in my head (they are pretty much my favorite Clan, though), so I wasn't quite sure which of the various Gangrel stereotypes you were aiming at. The problem I see with this is that &quot;avoiding fancy, formal affairs with suffocating rules&quot; basically means &quot;avoiding vampire society entirely,&quot; since vampires do love themselves lots of fancy formal affairs with suffocating rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't always run it that way. A bloodline of Gangrel are in charge of my game's city, for example, and Elysium is just hanging out in a tavern. There are some suits, but its mostly way more relaxed. Its Vancouver, so, between hipsters and the actual old school lumber industry, there's way more flannel than tuxedos. <br /> <br /> I have only rarely, if ever, ran Elysium as a super fancy debutante ball style thing. But, even still, I also explicitly made sure my new flaw wouldn't make Gangrel feel cornered in Elysium, or when taking Invictus Oaths. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852439#post852439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also essentially bars Gangrel from three or four of the five Covenants (depending on exactly how formal and suffocating you think the rules of the Ordo Dracul, Invictus, Circle, and Sanctum are.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to make it clear that restrictions you accepted willingly were ok. You can join any kind of pact, contract, oath, whatever, and willingly subject yourself to whatever rules you want. It's when you feel cornered--like the rules were not expected, or, someone twists the rules to catch you. <br /> <br /> Think of that trope in, well, a lot of different media, where the protagonist goes to some foreign land he doesn't understand and finds himself married due to some normally innocuous action he took. A Gangrel would feel cornered then, but not if they willingly chose to get married. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852439#post852439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that the Gangrel kind of embrace a pretty wide stereotype, so honing in on what, exactly, the Clan means is likely going to be different for everyone who reads them. &quot;Primal, animalistic vampire&quot; is far broader than &quot;Aristocratic power-hungry vampire&quot; or &quot;modern sexy vampire&quot; in a lot of ways. Maybe that's the stereotype that should be embraced. &quot;Primal animalism&quot; has a lot of different connotations, so maybe an array of Banes that the player picks one of, to reflect how the primal, animalistic nature of the Clan manifests in her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but again, my goal is to encourage the stereotype with negative space. If they act &quot;primal and animalistic,&quot; I don't want a flaw that says, &quot;You act primal and animalistic in X situation,&quot; I want a flaw that indirectly says, &quot;Acting primal and animalistic prevents you from having to deal with this flaw.&quot; <br /> <br /> Like I said at the beginning, it's like how Nosferatu just stop trying to relate to humans. They have social penalties to interact nicely, so, they, you know, don't. They avoid people or treat them aggressively or dishonestly, with intimidate or subterfuge or something unpenalized. Hence the lonely curse. I wouldn't want a flaw that just said, &quot;Oh, you must be lonely!&quot; I want playing up the stereotype to feel like winning, because you're avoiding your flaw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852461#post852461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was paraphrasing from the book.<br /> <br /> 'While frnezied, the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast's desires. She does so with immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon. If there's someone in the way, she throws him or decks him. If she's hungry, she bites the closest thing to her mouth. That said, the Beast isn't stupid. It's capable of doing the kind of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the predatory aura if that will help sate it.'<br /> <br /> Killing everything around you is more the domain of werewolf's Death Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so, ok, the 2nd example was hyperbolic, but, I'm sorry, in a frenzy, you do rip people's throats out before you just punch them. I re-read the section. Some choice quotes:<br /> <br /> &quot;When the vampire faces danger, hunger, or threat, the Beast goads her to immediate and extreme response, usually meaning a blood-soaked frenzy.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;When frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast's desires. She does so with immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Beast is &quot;capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predaor is.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, no, if you frenzied because a guy cornered you in a club (in this theoretical world where you could frenzy from something like that), your frenzy goal would be &quot;get this guy out of my face&quot; and the Beast wouldn't care that intimidation or just a shove would accomplish that, you would have an extreme response and act with destructive abandon like an enraged animal predator, resulting in a blood-soaked frenzy. The most destructive and assured way to get him out of your face is to use the frenzy's special bite+grapple rules. In the cage, your goal is to get out. You'd just flail and smash at the cage--you're not thinking about picking the lock or taunting a guy to open it. you're just frenzying and raging. My description went too far in scenario 2, ok, but I hope that one exaggeration hasn't destroyed my point.<br /> <br /> I don't think the condition I created is like a pseudo frenzy. I think it's much more flexible and open. Is that still being disputed? <br /> <br /> What else is bad about the condition, assuming I change it from being a Humanity cap to just penalized based on humanity? Does it not fit the theme? Will it not negatively reinforce the gangrel stereotype of being wild and free? Is it too vague? Is the idea good but I wrote it poorly? What's wrong with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T12:59:23-07:00","id":852552,"title":"","content":"Grappling and drinking someone isn't a way to get them out of the way, it's how you fulfill your hunger. You're not getting them out of the way, they're staying right there, and you're just closer now because you're drinking from them.<br /> <br /> Another example might be a confrontation with a galloi, who reveals their true self to you and spices it up with some Nightmare disciplines. Suddenly the skin on the vampire before you sloughs off revealing black mold within and fat worms ooze from the gaping holes where muscles once were. One pushes its eye out and the orb cracks on the floor releasing a smell like a rotten egg. You want to get out, you want to get away. 'Eat it' is not anywhere near the top of the list of ways to go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-24-2016, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:17:18-07:00","id":852558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852552#post852552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grappling and drinking someone isn't a way to get them out of the way, it's how you fulfill your hunger. You're not getting them out of the way, they're staying right there, and you're just closer now because you're drinking from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Biting them will kill them the fastest, though. It's the most damage you could do unarmed, for sure, and the most violent and destructive option. An angry animal isn't going to push you down, it's going to bite. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852552#post852552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another example might be a confrontation with a galloi, who reveals their true self to you and spices it up with some Nightmare disciplines. Suddenly the skin on the vampire before you sloughs off revealing black mold within and fat worms ooze from the gaping holes where muscles once were. One pushes its eye out and the orb cracks on the floor releasing a smell like a rotten egg. You want to get out, you want to get away. 'Eat it' is not anywhere near the top of the list of ways to go about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends. If they used Nightmare to make you fear frenzy, you're running away, for sure. If they're blocking your way, you're trying to get around them. Your goal is different--fear does not equal anger. When you're angry at a douchebag trapping your in a corner, you're not trying to run away afraid from him, you're <i>angry</i>. You want to fuck him up. <br /> <br /> Regardless, I don't want this to force a frenzy and my examples were just an extreme take on what would cause it. My real point keeps getting buried in side rules discussions. I was just trying to show that the condition I created wasn't like a psuedo frenzy, that's all. Do you still think it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T13:22:26-07:00","id":852561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852558#post852558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biting them will kill them the fastest, though. It's the most damage you could do unarmed, for sure, and the most violent and destructive option. An angry animal isn't going to push you down, it's going to bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>An angry animal is likely to shove past you if it wants to get away. Biting them to death is likely to take multiple turns of being there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It depends. If they used Nightmare to make you fear frenzy, you're running away, for sure. If they're blocking your way, you're trying to get around them. Your goal is different--fear does not equal anger. When you're angry at a douchebag trapping your in a corner, you're not trying to run away afraid from him, you're <i>angry</i>. You want to fuck him up.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I don't want this to force a frenzy and my examples were just an extreme take on what would cause it. My real point keeps getting buried in side rules discussions. I was just trying to show that the condition I created wasn't like a psuedo frenzy, that's all. Do you still think it is? </div> </div> </div>Yes. It looks like second edition's frenzy without the benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T14:28:49-07:00","id":852604,"title":"","content":"My Brujah character (yes, yes, wrong Vampire, I know) was once interrogating a ghoul, and said ghoul happened to say something he really, really shouldn't. So my character, in a frenzy, proceeded to grab the poor guy by the throat and slammed his face into the kitchen's marble countertop until the ghoul stopped twitching.<br /> <br /> Under your interpretation of the Frenzy rules, would this have happened?<br /> <br /> EDIT: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">To be fair, he did mention to a Brujah's face how much he had enjoyed killing said Brujah's soon-to-be childe.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","user":"Justin Sane","date":". 03-24-2016, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:35:22-07:00","id":852696,"title":"","content":"Remember what is the meta function of the Beast. It's the direct opposite of the masquerade and hiding. Its the temptation to stop pretending and ignore the rules that constrain you. Vampires are expected to pretend and obey the protocol; beast is the desite to just be and fuck the protocol.<br /> So you could frenzy and bite the dude. Or you could tear him down verbally and humiliate him. You can snap at someone with forceful abandon and inner rage without getting physical.<br /> Dont focus on the physical. Focus on the goal, and the fact that inner part of you really wants something here and now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T22:37:30-07:00","id":852814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852561#post852561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An angry animal is likely to shove past you if it wants to get away. Biting them to death is likely to take multiple turns of being there.</div> </div> </div> </div>An animal is only likely to shove past if its afraid and wants to get away. If, instead, it's angry at you for cornering it, it's going to bite the fuck out of you.<br /> <br /> I think the disconnect here is that I assumed the Beast would be angry about being trapped, and, maybe, you were thinking the Beast would be afraid of it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852561#post852561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. It looks like second edition's frenzy without the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really know what to do with this. I read and re-read the frenzy sections and came out with a beast that acts with violent abandon. I just don't see your reading of it at all. Or I don't understand how you're reading my condition.<br /> <br /> Do you think someone in frenzy in 2e can pick a lock? Seduce someone? Even talk coherently? Use disciplines that work indirectly, like Animalism 3? Actually, any non-physical discipline?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852604#post852604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Brujah character (yes, yes, wrong Vampire, I know) was once interrogating a ghoul, and said ghoul happened to say something he really, really shouldn't. So my character, in a frenzy, proceeded to grab the poor guy by the throat and slammed his face into the kitchen's marble countertop until the ghoul stopped twitching.<br /> <br /> Under your interpretation of the Frenzy rules, would this have happened?<br /> <br /> EDIT: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">To be fair, he did mention to a Brujah's face how much he had enjoyed killing said Brujah's soon-to-be childe.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>So, I think what you're getting at is the idea that your character grappled and slammed the guy rather than biting him, yeah?<br /> <br /> So, if I wanted to be totally perfectly consistent, I'd point out that in Masquerade, biting wasn't the most damage you could do (I also don't recall getting to bite and grapple in one action like you can in 2e here).<br /> <br /> But, really, no, I think that was fine and would be fine in 1e or 2e as well. You were excessively, brutally violent over a minor slight. That's the point of frenzy. Perfect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852696#post852696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember what is the meta function of the Beast. It's the direct opposite of the masquerade and hiding. Its the temptation to stop pretending and ignore the rules that constrain you. Vampires are expected to pretend and obey the protocol; beast is the desite to just be and fuck the protocol.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't get that at all. As far as I'm concerned, and as far as I read, the Beast is the contrast to Humanity, not to the Masquerade. It's the thing you're fighting to not become. You're struggling to stay human because the other option is animal. That's the trick of the whole thing--the Beast gives you awesome powers that could tempt you into thinking you're better than humans, but frenzy proves, no, you might become something less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852696#post852696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you could frenzy and bite the dude. Or you could tear him down verbally and humiliate him. You can snap at someone with forceful abandon and inner rage without getting physical.<br /> Dont focus on the physical. Focus on the goal, and the fact that inner part of you really wants something here and now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just...what? So, two responses here:<br /> <br /> 1) No, no, no. There's no way at all that frenzy will ever be that at my table. That's bizarre and not at all what frenzy should be. It's violent and terrible. You don't frenzy and throw your wine at someone's face, you frenzy and rip their face off. You don't frenzy and the caged animal roiling inside gets out and just calls someone a twat. You don't frenzy and yell. You frenzy and break things, rip things apart, run wild...if you're right about this, then I understand more of why people were telling me before to play 1e with some rules updates. I would absolutely not use that rule, I would be using previous edition frenzies for sure.<br /> <br /> 2) I just can't conceive of how you could be right though. I read and re-read this book's frenzy sections. &quot;Blood-soaked frenzy.&quot; &quot;Immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon.&quot; &quot;Capable of the things an enraged terrified or starving animal predator is.&quot; None of those words suggest I can just yell at someone and satisfy the Beast. Where is this in the book that you're seeing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 03-25-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T23:17:15-07:00","id":852832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852814#post852814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An animal is only likely to shove past if its afraid and wants to get away. If, instead, it's angry at you for cornering it, it's going to bite the fuck out of you.<br /> <br /> I think the disconnect here is that I assumed the Beast would be angry about being trapped, and, maybe, you were thinking the Beast would be afraid of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your first example isn't the kind of thing that would start a frenzy, but even if it did, it is not a killing frenzy, or a feeding frenzy. This person did not kill your last touchstone and you didn't just walk on them desecrating their grave. They're an obstruction, you move the obstruction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't really know what to do with this. I read and re-read the frenzy sections and came out with a beast that acts with violent abandon. I just don't see your reading of it at all. Or I don't understand how you're reading my condition.<br /> <br /> Do you think someone in frenzy in 2e can pick a lock? Seduce someone? Even talk coherently? Use disciplines that work indirectly, like Animalism 3? Actually, any non-physical discipline? </div> </div> </div>Your Condition didn't seem like it would allow for seducing someone or even talking coherently, maybe in a rushed stammering. Picking a lock, maybe, but with the Condition or with frenzy a brute force attempt seems more likely. Nonetheless, I don't believe its exactly the same as frenzy, it just seems a very much like frenzy. You have to do something, which is what frenzy is about. It's a bit like the soft rage of werewolf.<br /> <br /> As has been established, frenzy is not just about killing everything in your path. If you choose to have it mean that in your game, that's great, and certainly makes your Condition different. But you should appreciate that not everyone knows the rules to your game and the rules in the book are pretty clear about those things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T08:58:40-07:00","id":852995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR2E p104</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Upon entering frenzy, determine what the Beast wants. Does it want to escape? Does it want to punish the person who insulted his host? Does it want blood? Typically, <b>frenzy ends when that thing occurs</b>.<br /> <br /> While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. She does so with immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon. <b>If there\u2019s someone in the way, she throws him or decks him</b>. If she\u2019s hungry, she bites the closest thing to her mouth. <b>That said, the Beast isn\u2019t stupid</b>. It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is, and it will lash out with the predatory aura if that will help sate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. I don't think we really need to link nature videos of all the ways animals use warning signs to get other things to back the hell off, without resorting to a grapple/bite combo. Hissing, growling, standing on back legs, etc. If this gets the opponent to back off without a fight - that is what the animal will do. Frenzy is the mode of the predator beast, using the tools at its disposal to get what it wants. It isn't rabies - <i>unless - </i>that's how the player wants to portray it.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't stop a player from draining four humans in a scene after a hunger frenzy and just burning the excess blood for physical intensity. Nor would I stop the player who feeds up to his maximum on one, then argues that the frenzy goal has been met and doesn't attack the rest. They are both valid choices, in my book, and I think the reading supports that. My disconnect with your interpretation is that it seems like you are saying you wouldn't allow the second option.<br /> <br /> Vampire goes into a (fear) frenzy after being cornered in an alley. There's a homeless man in between the vampire and the only way out. If one player wanted to bite him, draw blood, then throw him down, that's fine. If another wanted to lash out with the Monstrous beast and intimidate him with a growl or a shout - I'd also allow that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:08:50-07:00","id":853003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852832#post852832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your first example isn't the kind of thing that would start a frenzy, but even if it did, it is not a killing frenzy, or a feeding frenzy. This person did not kill your last touchstone and you didn't just walk on them desecrating their grave. They're an obstruction, you move the obstruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of my example was, &quot;What if, instead of giving this condition, being confined just caused a frenzy?&quot; The book describes three kinds of frenzy: angry, scared, and hungry. It doesn't describe an &quot;obstructed&quot; frenzy. <br /> <br /> &quot;When the vampire faces danger, hunger, or threat...&quot; <br /> <br /> I did not interpret this guy as danger, I interpreted him as threat.<br /> <br /> &quot;Upon entering frenzy, determine what the Beast wants. Does it want to escape? Does it want to punish the person who insulted his host? Does it want blood?&quot;<br /> <br /> Again, three options are presented. Since this guy trapping you isn't a danger, I assumed the frenzy would be to punish him, not to escape. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852832#post852832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Condition didn't seem like it would allow for seducing someone or even talking coherently, maybe in a rushed stammering.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you would have to spend a willpower to seduce someone, but, just one, not one per turn (which would basically mean &quot;you don't have enough willpower to seduce someone while frenzying.&quot; I am stunned it came across that you couldn't speak coherently or had to do so in a rushed stammering. I can't figure that one out. How could I word it better so you don't think this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852832#post852832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Picking a lock, maybe, but with the Condition or with frenzy a brute force attempt seems more likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>You think a frenzying vampire can potentially pick a lock? &quot;An enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator&quot; can pick a lock (also note, three options--anger, fear, or hunger)? Why do you think a brute force attempt is more likely with the condition? You don't lose your self at all in any way. You have full faculty, you just take a penalty and must spend willpower to do anything that won't <i>directly</i> lead to you remedying your confinement. So, picking a lock would, totally directly lead to removing confinement, no question. That would be fine. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852832#post852832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nonetheless, I don't believe its exactly the same as frenzy, it just seems a very much like frenzy. You have to do something, which is what frenzy is about. It's a bit like the soft rage of werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to do something, or rather, are strongly encouraged to do something, but that thing is open ended and you have your full wits about you. You're able to take any action at your disposal that works, rather than &quot;run, kill, or eat.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852832#post852832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As has been established, frenzy is not just about killing everything in your path. If you choose to have it mean that in your game, that's great, and certainly makes your Condition different. But you should appreciate that not everyone knows the rules to your game and the rules in the book are pretty clear about those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I'm having trouble with. I'm more than ready to say, &quot;yes, I houserule a lot of stuff.&quot; But, I've read this frenzy section like 10 times in the past two days, and the book is very clear that <i>its a violent, aggressive state</i>. It specifically says a blood-soaked frenzy is likely. You frenzy to run away, to punish (in an excessively violent, no concern for consequences way), or to eat. You don't frenzy to &quot;aggressively debate someone&quot; or even &quot;push someone down without otherwise hurting them.&quot; I just absolutely do not see any references in the book that suggests frenzy is anything but awful and excessively violent.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you automatically kill everyone, and having a guy unconscious on the ground is probably enough (you won't finish him, for example) but you're not going to choose a non-damaging option when you have a very damaging opportunity available. Blood soaked frenzy. You're going to do what Justin Sane's Brujah did and slam the guy's head into the bar until he stops twitching, not slap him and storm off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:20:52-07:00","id":853010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852995#post852995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Emphasis mine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The guy in the way in your reference is not the <i>target</i> of the frenzy, he's just in the way. Yes, you'll throw a guy across the room to rip the throat out of the guy behind him, or to desperately tear out the door away from the fire like a bat out of hell, or run <i>into</i> the door away from the sun. But you don't throw a guy and then say, &quot;ok, done!&quot; Frenzy ends when that thing occurs, but that thing is never &quot;throw this guy down.&quot; That's not a thing worth frenzying over. Frenzy is flee, punish, or eat, not &quot;push down.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852995#post852995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we really need to link nature videos of all the ways animals use warning signs to get other things to back the hell off, without resorting to a grapple/bite combo. Hissing, growling, standing on back legs, etc. If this gets the opponent to back off without a fight - that is what the animal will do. Frenzy is the mode of the predator beast, using the tools at its disposal to get what it wants. It isn't rabies - <i>unless - </i>that's how the player wants to portray it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those things are for a frightened animal. Enraged animals don't hiss and growl, they bite and claw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852995#post852995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't stop a player from draining four humans in a scene after a hunger frenzy and just burning the excess blood for physical intensity. Nor would I stop the player who feeds up to his maximum on one, then argues that the frenzy goal has been met and doesn't attack the rest. They are both valid choices, in my book, and I think the reading supports that. My disconnect with your interpretation is that it seems like you are saying you wouldn't allow the second option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, with hunger frenzy, I would suggest the 2nd option is more correct. Frenzy ends when the Beast gets what it wants, after all. If the vampire was under <i>anger frenzy, </i>though, and all four guys were part of the provocation, you're not going to push them down and then walk away, no, they're all going to end up broken and bleeding if they stick around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=852995#post852995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire goes into a (fear) frenzy after being cornered in an alley. There's a homeless man in between the vampire and the only way out. If one player wanted to bite him, draw blood, then throw him down, that's fine. If another wanted to lash out with the Monstrous beast and intimidate him with a growl or a shout - I'd also allow that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is exactly what I've been saying...the disconnect is not that we think differently about frenzy, exactly, it's this weird idea that (in this theoreticaly houserule I don't want to use and only made up in the first place to contrast with the one I was actually proposing) being cornered by a homeless guy would cause a fear frenzy and not an anger one at being cornered by such an insignificant shit. I was assuming anger frenzy. I was not thinking, &quot;Oh no, this guy at the bar is dangerous I need to get away,&quot; I was thinking, &quot;How dare this shithead pin me in a corner.&quot; Either way, I don't want to cause frenzy with my house ruled Gangrel bane, so, the point is moot. The only reason I came up with those scenarios was to show how my condition <i>wasn't</i> like Frenzy. It certainly looks more like fear frenzy than anger frenzy, but fear frenzy is reserved for fire and sunlight, yeah? Maybe weird supernatural powers? For things that are actually a threat to a vampire, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":". 03-25-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:23:00-07:00","id":853012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853003#post853003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of my example was, &quot;What if, instead of giving this condition, being confined just caused a frenzy?&quot; The book describes three kinds of frenzy: angry, scared, and hungry. It doesn't describe an &quot;obstructed&quot; frenzy.<br /> <br /> &quot;When the vampire faces danger, hunger, or threat...&quot;<br /> <br /> I did not interpret this guy as danger, I interpreted him as threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe any but the most paranoid and low-Humanity vampires would see that as a threat. And even fewer would consider it a threat that needs to be killed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, you would have to spend a willpower to seduce someone, but, just one, not one per turn (which would basically mean &quot;you don't have enough willpower to seduce someone while frenzying.&quot; I am stunned it came across that you couldn't speak coherently or had to do so in a rushed stammering. I can't figure that one out. How could I word it better so you don't think this?<br /> <br /> You think a frenzying vampire can potentially pick a lock? &quot;An enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator&quot; can pick a lock (also note, three options--anger, fear, or hunger)? Why do you think a brute force attempt is more likely with the condition? You don't lose your self at all in any way. You have full faculty, you just take a penalty and must spend willpower to do anything that won't <i>directly</i> lead to you remedying your confinement. So, picking a lock would, totally directly lead to removing confinement, no question. That would be fine. </div> </div> </div>I was referring to your confinement Condition. As I've noted, it seems 'like' frenzy. You have to spend a Willpower to do anything that is not getting out of the spot you're in as soon as possible. This implies two things. One, it is hard to do anything but try to escape. Two, even the most strongwilled of vampires has a limited range of things they can do beyond try to escape. Under this kind of pressure, lock-picking and talking coherently don't seem like something you could do without extra effort. Gangrel chafe and lash out. Not calmly ask people to set them free or meticulously pick locks. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is what I'm having trouble with. I'm more than ready to say, &quot;yes, I houserule a lot of stuff.&quot; But, I've read this frenzy section like 10 times in the past two days, and the book is very clear that <i>its a violent, aggressive state</i>. It specifically says a blood-soaked frenzy is likely. You frenzy to run away, to punish (in an excessively violent, no concern for consequences way), or to eat. You don't frenzy to &quot;aggressively debate someone&quot; or even &quot;push someone down without otherwise hurting them.&quot; I just absolutely do not see any references in the book that suggests frenzy is anything but awful and excessively violent.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you automatically kill everyone, and having a guy unconscious on the ground is probably enough (you won't finish him, for example) but you're not going to choose a non-damaging option when you have a very damaging opportunity available. Blood soaked frenzy. You're going to do what Justin Sane's Brujah did and slam the guy's head into the bar until he stops twitching, not slap him and storm off. </div> </div> </div>It also says, 'If there's someone in the way, she throws them or decks them.' Not every vampire is going to kill everyone in their path whenever they're going to frenzy. If you're frenzying about getting away from a source of danger, or getting to something, wasting time killing people is going against the entire point of the frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:31:59-07:00","id":853022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853012#post853012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe any but the most paranoid and low-Humanity vampires would see that as a threat. And even fewer would consider it a threat that needs to be killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's certainly not a danger, so, there's no way it'd be a fear frenzy. You're not hungry. Angry is the only one left. And again, it was a theoretical houserule I don't even want to use. I was assuming it'd default to anger frenzy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853012#post853012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was referring to your confinement Condition. As I've noted, it seems 'like' frenzy. You have to spend a Willpower to do anything that is not getting out of the spot you're in as soon as possible. This implies two things. One, it is hard to do anything but try to escape. Two, even the most strongwilled of vampires has a limited range of things they can do beyond try to escape. Under this kind of pressure, lock-picking and talking coherently don't seem like something you could do without extra effort. Gangrel chafe and lash out. Not calmly ask people to set them free or meticulously pick locks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so, I need to fix the wording. That's helpful. How can I word it so you can take any action you're capable of with full faculty and reason, including speech and powers, but still can't just be cool with being confined without spending willpower to force themselves? How can I fix it so, to you, and others here, it does not resemble frenzy, but still heavily encourages getting out of confinement?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853012#post853012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also says, 'If there's someone in the way, she throws them or decks them.' Not every vampire is going to kill everyone in their path whenever they're going to frenzy. If you're frenzying about getting away from a source of danger, or getting to something, wasting time killing people is going against the entire point of the frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, again, you throw a guy out of your way to get to your goal. Yes. But when your goal is &quot;punish this guy&quot; you don't just push him down, you rip his throat out. Again, the disconnect was fear vs. anger frenzy, not &quot;uh oh, he doesn't understand frenzy!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:40:49-07:00","id":853028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853010#post853010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The guy in the way in your reference is not the <i>target</i> of the frenzy, he's just in the way. Yes, you'll throw a guy across the room to rip the throat out of the guy behind him, or to desperately tear out the door away from the fire like a bat out of hell, or run <i>into</i> the door away from the sun. But you don't throw a guy and then say, &quot;ok, done!&quot; Frenzy ends when that thing occurs, but that thing is never &quot;throw this guy down.&quot; That's not a thing worth frenzying over. Frenzy is flee, punish, or eat, not &quot;push down.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. However, your previous point where 'punish' does not 100% equate to 'kill' I think holds true. You would allow the frenzied kindred to drop out once the target was unconscious. I'd also allow the frenzy to end if the kindred clawed the target's face and they immediately capitulated in an obvious or physical way. Violence, yes. Blood, yes. Mindless killing machine, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853010#post853010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those things are for a frightened animal. Enraged animals don't hiss and growl, they bite and claw.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're trapping yourself too much in the 1E/Masq frenzy mindset, and not thinking how the animal kingdom actually works. Most fights between enraged predators are resolved pretty quickly, as one side backs the hell off because they are less invested in whatever is happening, be it territory, food, danger. My understanding (admittedly from TV, I'm not a biologist) is that knock-down drag-out fights between animals until one isn't moving are actually uncommon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853010#post853010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, with hunger frenzy, I would suggest the 2nd option is more correct. Frenzy ends when the Beast gets what it wants, after all. If the vampire was under <i>anger frenzy, </i>though, and all four guys were part of the provocation, you're not going to push them down and then walk away, no, they're all going to end up broken and bleeding if they stick around.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think making an example out of the leader with violence or lashing out with the Monstrous beast so that the group disperses or is cowed is also an acceptable end of the frenzy. And I think the reading would support that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853010#post853010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, this is exactly what I've been saying...the disconnect is not that we think differently about frenzy, exactly, is this weird idea that being cornered by a homeless guy would cause a fear frenzy and not an anger one at being cornered by such an insignificant shit. I was assuming anger frenzy. I was not thinking, &quot;Oh no, this guy at the bar is dangerous I need to get away,&quot; I was thinking, &quot;How dare this shithead pin me in a corner.&quot; Either way, I don't want to cause frenzy with my house ruled Gangrel bane, so, the point is moot. The only reason I came up with those scenarios was to show how my condition <i>wasn't</i> like Frenzy. It certainly looks more like fear frenzy than anger frenzy, but fear frenzy is reserved for fire and sunlight, yeah? Maybe weird supernatural powers? For things that are actually a threat to a vampire, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fire and Sunlight are easy examples, as well as damage from banes, and disciplines or devotions that force a frenzy with a flee agenda. However, any thing could be a threat to the vampire. Exceptional success on an intimidation roll? Any sort of damage that knocks you close to torpor? Being absolutely humiliated and yelled at by your Regnant for screwing up a mission? I think those are all within bounds to see if the player wants to make a frenzy check with a run-away agenda. Further, I think these opportunities create a lot more interesting scenes - how does the Ventrue CEO deal with the fact his beast just peed itself in the face of a high-BP boss? <br /> <br /> Again, you lose something when you try to convert the 2E mindset of <i>mechanics to support drama</i> into an exhaustive list with no wiggle room on implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T09:50:51-07:00","id":853033,"title":"","content":"I feel like you are too focused on &quot;types&quot; of Frenzy. There is no such thing as a &quot;fear frenzy&quot; or &quot;anger frenzy&quot; in 2e. There is just frenzy. The goal is more important. Ask yourself instead &quot;What does the Beast want right now?&quot;<br /> <br /> So when a vampire is cornered and provoked to Frenzy somehow (hyperfocusing on this example seems also not good; as has been said, this scenario wouldn't likely trigger it to begin with), you don't go &quot;what type of frenzy is this? anger frenzy&quot; you go &quot;what does the Beast want right now? It's cornered, and it wants to not be. It wants to stop being cornered.&quot; That answer defines how the vampire acts while frenzying. The vampire will do whatever it takes to stop being cornered. This could be anything from Lashing Out + Intimidate (the book explicitly says Predatory Aura is a valid means to the Frenzy's ends) to, yes, murdering the person in the way. That's up to PC interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T10:14:01-07:00","id":853045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Cornered Beast</i><br /> <br /> <i>You feel trapped and must escape at all costs. The closer your Beast lies to the surface, the worse this feeling becomes, as the devil inside seethes with resentment at your confinement. You must take direct action, either to escape the situation or to lash out at your perceived captors. All other non-reflexive actions require a willpower point to attempt and are capped by your Humanity. Rolls to resist frenzy suffer a penalty equal to the penalty you suffer on social rolls relating to humans due to low Humanity.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Possible Sources: The Gangrel clan bane</i><br /> <i>Resolution: Frenzy or escape the confinement that triggered this condition</i><br /> <i>Beat: n/a</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> In any case, apologies for the derail. I just find concept discussions like this enjoyably fascinating, and I appreciate your responses. In regards to your actual question re: the condition. Obviously it's going to have to be a judgment call on when you should apply the condition. I'd start off easy, erring on the side of it not applying in the edge cases until you have a chance to work it in some.<br /> <br /> For the mechanics, I think the Spend WP and Capped by Humanity combo is too harsh. Did they keep any &quot;Capped by Humanity&quot; mechanics in 2E? If not, I'd ditch it entirely.<br /> <br /> For the Spending Willpower, I can see the point that was made for it being just kind of a mini-frenzy. &quot;When &lt;triggered&gt; you must act in a specific, direct way. If you want to do anything else, you must spend 1 WP to take the contrary action.&quot; Statement describes both Frenzy and Cornered Beast.<br /> <br /> Other limiting options in lieu of humanity caps:<ul><li>May not spend Willpower on extra effort for actions not related to getting away.</li> <li>Others who attempt to influence or manipulate your character into taking an action that would end the confinement score an exceptional success on (3) instead of (5) successes.</li> </ul>For example, a Gangrel has been brought in chains before the prince for a crime he didn't commit. One of the PCs is the 'prosecutor' for the case. The PC offers the Gangrel to get everything over with right now if they just admit their guilt, and accept a punishment of losing their fangs for one month. Let the PC make the social / mental / maneuver roll per your style, and only require the three successes for a big win. Or, you're confined in an alleyway, but your terrible foe is also there. Cornered Beast wants you to get out, but you really want to kill this guy. He Dominates you to run away when he sees the murder in your eyes - and it's easier for him to do so.<br /> <br /> I think the <i>must spend willpower</i> bit would worries me most because it sounds like your game doesn't treat WP as fluidly as 2E, and I'd worry about Gangrel getting hit too often, or placed in confinement such that they run out of WP and can't do anything useful. Could the Gangrel in jail start seducing one of the guards in hopes they might let them out? Or would that require a Willpower vs. Just pounding on the reinforced steel door, even if they already tried that and failed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T10:47:33-07:00","id":853059,"title":"","content":"As Maina said - there's no types of frenzy. There was such a thing in 1e, where we had the anger, hunger and fear frenzy, but not anymore. Now it's just frenzy with the condition set to being the most appropriate. Which could as well be - get there (meanwhile shove him out of the way), or whatever else the Beast thinks is needed the most at the moment. You don't have to kill anyone unless that is a must to your true objective (and killing someone is rarely the objective, more often it will be to show your own superiority, to injure, to WIN, to survive, to feed your hunger). Killing is a tool for the beast, not the goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T11:29:38-07:00","id":853078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. However, your previous point where 'punish' does not 100% equate to 'kill' I think holds true. You would allow the frenzied kindred to drop out once the target was unconscious. I'd also allow the frenzy to end if the kindred clawed the target's face and they immediately capitulated in an obvious or physical way. Violence, yes. Blood, yes. Mindless killing machine, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with that. I just don't expect people not used to vampires would realize that capitulating is going to save them. I feel like most of the time, they'd just think, &quot;holy crap, I'm going to die!&quot; Even if they did just obviously capitulate, though, biting or worse, clawing a guy that survives the attack is a worse masquerade breach than if you just had finished him. The guy is going to have been close enough and felt enough to know you bit/clawed him, whereas bystanders might have just thought you had a hidden knife or something, maybe, or a broken glass they didn't see. It's bad no matter what.<br /> <br /> But I should stop bringing up this hypothetical situation using a hypothetical rule...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're trapping yourself too much in the 1E/Masq frenzy mindset, and not thinking how the animal kingdom actually works. Most fights between enraged predators are resolved pretty quickly, as one side backs the hell off because they are less invested in whatever is happening, be it territory, food, danger. My understanding (admittedly from TV, I'm not a biologist) is that knock-down drag-out fights between animals until one isn't moving are actually uncommon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between two predators confronting each other, yeah, because both are in danger and taking too much damage is going to weaken you more than the victory will strengthen you. You might kill this rival, but if he got a good bite/claw in, you're still bleeding and will probably die, or at least be too weak to fight off the next rival. So, yes, posturing is a big thing animals do, and I imagine it's a big thing vampires do, too. But I view that posturing as Lashing Out, not as frenzy. Frenzy is something else. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I think making an example out of the leader with violence or lashing out with the Monstrous beast so that the group disperses or is cowed is also an acceptable end of the frenzy. And I think the reading would support that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that depends heavily on the situation. Was there even an obvious leader? What specifically was the provocation? Are these humans, ghouls, or vampires? I feel like &quot;dispersing the crowd&quot; is a weird goal for the Beast to have. I think &quot;punish the idiots that harassed me&quot; is a lot more likely, if they're humans, and &quot;get the hell away from here&quot; is more likely if they're vampires. <br /> <br /> If they are people, and they all drop to their knees right away, ok, maybe no violence, but if they don't break and run or throw themselves down in submission, there will be blood. Note that I think typical human gang thug reaction would not be those things--it would be to fight back until one of their number goes down horrifically, then break and run, unless cornered and unable, in which case, bowel voiding and submission might occur.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exceptional success on an intimidation roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoah, what? A mundane snarly guy can send a vampire fleeing like a baby? I don't think so...that feels way off. Exceptional success can create a condition, maybe Shaken, but not a frenzy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any sort of damage that knocks you close to torpor?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that could go 50/50, fear or anger, depending on whether you considered the enemy a credible threat or just one audacious enough to stand up against you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being absolutely humiliated and yelled at by your Regnant for screwing up a mission?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I can't picture that, either. &quot;You suck!&quot; &quot;Waaaaaah!&quot; No, that feels off, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think those are all within bounds to see if the player wants to make a frenzy check with a run-away agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the player wants to? Huh? Is this a story game thing where people actually want to frenzy sometimes?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Further, I think these opportunities create a lot more interesting scenes - how does the Ventrue CEO deal with the fact his beast just peed itself in the face of a high-BP boss?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think the Beast would be more likely to fail horribly at ripping his boss's face off, but, I really also don't see the Beast getting involved here anyway.<br /> <br /> That said, I won't dispute these things. These things, at least, I can see being in the text. I don't see the idea of anger frenzying and just pushing someone over, though. I see blood soaked, excessively violent frenzying as the default assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853028#post853028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, you lose something when you try to convert the 2E mindset of <i>mechanics to support drama</i> into an exhaustive list with no wiggle room on implementation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess. I just want mechanics to support a consistent world, where stuff works in a predictable fashion, not just &quot;whatever is most dramatic.&quot; Drama happens on its own, I don't want to artificially create it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853033#post853033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like you are too focused on &quot;types&quot; of Frenzy. There is no such thing as a &quot;fear frenzy&quot; or &quot;anger frenzy&quot; in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, except that every time examples are given, they are given in threes, and they always line up perfectly with fear, anger, and hunger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853033#post853033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So when a vampire is cornered and provoked to Frenzy somehow (hyperfocusing on this example seems also not good; as has been said, this scenario wouldn't likely trigger it to begin with), you don't go &quot;what type of frenzy is this? anger frenzy&quot; you go &quot;what does the Beast want right now? It's cornered, and it wants to not be. It wants to stop being cornered.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree hyperfocusing here is bad, and that this is the disconnect. I don't think, in this improperly hyperfocused example, that the Beast wants to not be cornered, I think it wants to punish the guy that cornered it. &quot;Nobody puts baby in a corner, damnit!&quot; Not, &quot;oh my gosh, I'm scared of this corner! Eek! Run!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853033#post853033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That answer defines how the vampire acts while frenzying. The vampire will do whatever it takes to stop being cornered. This could be anything from Lashing Out + Intimidate (the book explicitly says Predatory Aura is a valid means to the Frenzy's ends) to, yes, murdering the person in the way. That's up to PC interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book says lashing out is acceptable, but I have yet to figure out a way that Lashing Out could help a frenzy accomplish it goal except maybe to reduce their defense with Monstrous beast? I don't know. Intimidation is a waste of a Beast's time, I would think. Why do that when you could be removing their organs instead? They'll be just as afraid, I assure you, and will be just as likely, if not more likely, to flee when missing chunks than when you just growl or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In any case, apologies for the derail. I just find concept discussions like this enjoyably fascinating, and I appreciate your responses.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting, usually, but this particular one got too caught up on, well, practically straw men I built to contrast my condition with against frenzy, not any real situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In regards to your actual question re: the condition. Obviously it's going to have to be a judgment call on when you should apply the condition. I'd start off easy, erring on the side of it not applying in the edge cases until you have a chance to work it in some.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I actually expect it to be very rarely come up. It's not a common occurence--it is difficult to corner a vampire who doesn't want to be cornered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the mechanics, I think the Spend WP and Capped by Humanity combo is too harsh. Did they keep any &quot;Capped by Humanity&quot; mechanics in 2E? If not, I'd ditch it entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the previous Gangrel flaw is capping their rolls to resist frenzy by their Humanity. That said, someone else mentioned this and I feel changing it to be a penalty based on your Humanity (i.e. the same as your social penalty) is a fine alternative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Spending Willpower, I can see the point that was made for it being just kind of a mini-frenzy. &quot;When &lt;triggered&gt; you must act in a specific, direct way. If you want to do anything else, you must spend 1 WP to take the contrary action.&quot; Statement describes both Frenzy and Cornered Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, sure. I think the difference is that you're fully in control and have access to your full range of capabilities and reason. And the willpower is per action, not round, so actions that take more than 3-6 seconds are actually doable cheaply/at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May not spend Willpower on extra effort for actions not related to getting away.</div> </div> </div> </div>That just seems too weak. Oh, ok, I see that in a &quot;normal&quot; game it wouldn't be, because people can spend willpower constantly without fear of running out, but in my game without Anchors and just getting it back for resting and major accomplishments of awesome, Willpower is a carefully guarded resource, so, they're not going to be throwing it around every scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Others who attempt to influence or manipulate your character into taking an action that would end the confinement score an exceptional success on (3) instead of (5) successes.[/LIST]For example, a Gangrel has been brought in chains before the prince for a crime he didn't commit. One of the PCs is the 'prosecutor' for the case. The PC offers the Gangrel to get everything over with right now if they just admit their guilt, and accept a punishment of losing their fangs for one month. Let the PC make the social / mental / maneuver roll per your style, and only require the three successes for a big win.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this might be another case of unwitting houserules, but the prosecutor wouldn't roll anything there at my table. They'd present the offer and the Gangrel would decide, based on the offer, what to do. Why would you roll? Social skills aren't mind control and you're not persuading anyone of anything, you're just offering a trade and seeing if they accept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Or, you're confined in an alleyway, but your terrible foe is also there. Cornered Beast wants you to get out, but you really want to kill this guy. He Dominates you to run away when he sees the murder in your eyes - and it's easier for him to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand your point (though I think that since Dominate takes two rounds to get you to run, that he's unlikely to succeed), but I don't think this is enough to count as a Clan Bane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853045#post853045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the <i>must spend willpower</i> bit would worries me most because it sounds like your game doesn't treat WP as fluidly as 2E, and I'd worry about Gangrel getting hit too often, or placed in confinement such that they run out of WP and can't do anything useful. Could the Gangrel in jail start seducing one of the guards in hopes they might let them out? Or would that require a Willpower vs. Just pounding on the reinforced steel door, even if they already tried that and failed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that this condition will happen enough to cause that problem, but I can see the concern. I think a jailed Gangrel losing all their willpower feels appropriate, honestly, but super rare anyway. Do you know how hard it is to put a vampire in jail without torporing them? <br /> <br /> That said, it would depend. If the Gangrel had reason to believe the guard had a key on their person and could get to that key via seduction, yeah, that'd work without cost in my mind.<br /> <br /> But, ok, let's say I take away the Willpower Cost and change the penalty from being capped by Humanity to being equal to your social penalty, does that still work? What about at Humanity 6 when your clan bane first activates, but you have no social penalty yet? I feel like it needs more teeth than that. If Willpower is too high a cost, what else can I do? <br /> <br /> Do you have an alternative suggestion that accomplishes a similar goal of making the Gangrel feel wild and free because they are avoiding their clan's bane? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:21:40-07:00","id":853188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853078#post853078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the player wants to? Huh? Is this a story game thing where people actually want to frenzy sometimes</div> </div> </div> </div>That frenzy I mentioned on my character? 100% my idea, I even asked the ST if we could assume the roll had failed. Just so you keep in mind that, for some of us, this *is* a story game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you have an alternative suggestion that accomplishes a similar goal of making the Gangrel feel wild and free because they are avoiding their clan's bane? </div> </div> </div>I get where you're coming from, but have you considered what you're trying to do might be impossible?<br /> <br /> On one hand, you're right. Trying their best to avoid their clan bane does push vampires into one of their clan's stereotypes. On the other hand, assuming &quot;all vampires avoid their clan banes&quot; eliminates many, otherwise viable, character concepts, like the Daeva with his prized herd or the Nosferatu socialite.<br /> <br /> Let me suggest an alternative: the Gangrel are viewed as wild and free because, unlike other clans, they *embrace* their bane. Knowing that at any time, they can call upon the Beast inside them, feels liberating to the Gangrel. Why should they listen to &quot;rules&quot; when they *know* they could rip out the messenger's throat if they wanted to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T15:35:34-07:00","id":853195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853078#post853078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the player wants to? Huh? Is this a story game thing where people actually want to frenzy sometimes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. Yes, conflict being the nature of drama and all that. However, even in the by-your-definition non-story games I've been in, I've seen players who have wanted to frenzy for various reasons. But still, I tend to prompt my players, &quot;This stressful enough to trigger a frenzy check?&quot; Nine times out of ten either they agree or have a legit counterpoint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853078#post853078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, this might be another case of unwitting houserules, but the prosecutor wouldn't roll anything there at my table. They'd present the offer and the Gangrel would decide, based on the offer, what to do. Why would you roll? Social skills aren't mind control and you're not persuading anyone of anything, you're just offering a trade and seeing if they accept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering they have specific rules for Persuasion, Fast-Talk, Intimidation, etc, I absolutely allow players to make social rolls to try and influence situations, not just them roleplaying and my own fiat on what happens. But this is a huge gaming agenda conversation. Maybe you thought I meant PC on PC, which is one of the places they specifically call out that you should decide how to use social rolls in those scenarios, from by the book to role-play only. But a PC prosecutor against an NPC Gangrel? You wouldn't let them roll anything? At that point, what's the point of low humanity penalties on social rolls against mortals, or the Nosferatu bane?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853078#post853078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, ok, let's say I take away the Willpower Cost and change the penalty from being capped by Humanity to being equal to your social penalty, does that still work? What about at Humanity 6 when your clan bane first activates, but you have no social penalty yet? I feel like it needs more teeth than that. If Willpower is too high a cost, what else can I do?<br /> <br /> Do you have an alternative suggestion that accomplishes a similar goal of making the Gangrel feel wild and free because they are avoiding their clan's bane?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's actually only going to come up very rarely, then I withdraw my objection. I was thinking along the lines that it would be as common as Daeva feeding or Nosferatu interacting with people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T17:41:14-07:00","id":853245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853188#post853188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get where you're coming from, but have you considered what you're trying to do might be impossible?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, not a possibility I am a fan of, but one nonetheless. The good news is, I can just leave things as is if I can't get it to work.<br /> <br /> And the Gangrel PC in the party is still Humanity 7 (they all are, actually), so, the Bane hasn't come up, yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853188#post853188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On one hand, you're right. Trying their best to avoid their clan bane does push vampires into one of their clan's stereotypes. On the other hand, assuming &quot;all vampires avoid their clan banes&quot; eliminates many, otherwise viable, character concepts, like the Daeva with his prized herd or the Nosferatu socialite.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it just makes those character types correctly subversions of tropes. They are the exception to prove the rule. Still totally possible, but not the default.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853188#post853188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me suggest an alternative: the Gangrel are viewed as wild and free because, unlike other clans, they *embrace* their bane. Knowing that at any time, they can call upon the Beast inside them, feels liberating to the Gangrel. Why should they listen to &quot;rules&quot; when they *know* they could rip out the messenger's throat if they wanted to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's no real way to embrace their Bane as is. Anyone is exactly as likely to act the same way, but the Gangrel among them will just so happen to frenzy more often. That's not really a predictable pattern or anything. It doesn't create a wild and bestial stereotype at all. Their default bane just creates a situation where more detached Gangrel have a hair trigger. That's all. Not wild, free, bestial, or anything, just more angry, scared, and hungry. Not interesting to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853195#post853195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh. Yes, conflict being the nature of drama and all that. However, even in the by-your-definition non-story games I've been in, I've seen players who have wanted to frenzy for various reasons. But still, I tend to prompt my players, &quot;This stressful enough to trigger a frenzy check?&quot; Nine times out of ten either they agree or have a legit counterpoint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just say, &quot;Roll Resolve + Composure - X&quot; because the point of frenzy is that it's against your will. Granted, with newfound knowledge that you can't Ride the Wave on purpose to frenzy at any time, you can only Ride the Wave in response to a frenzy provocation already present, that might change a little. But yeah, I would never, ever want to frenzy as a PC. The only reason I can come up with as to why you'd want to frenzy is because you think it'd be a cool story moment. So, it kind of requires a step out from your character and into the director/writer chair.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853195#post853195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering they have specific rules for Persuasion, Fast-Talk, Intimidation, etc, I absolutely allow players to make social rolls to try and influence situations, not just them roleplaying and my own fiat on what happens. But this is a huge gaming agenda conversation. Maybe you thought I meant PC on PC, which is one of the places they specifically call out that you should decide how to use social rolls in those scenarios, from by the book to role-play only. But a PC prosecutor against an NPC Gangrel? You wouldn't let them roll anything? At that point, what's the point of low humanity penalties on social rolls against mortals, or the Nosferatu bane?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is going to be another tangential side debate, I'm sure, but, in general, I dislike rolling for social stuff as a first resort.<br /> <br /> Now, in your specific example I would <i>especially</i> not roll anything, because you're not trying to convince, fast talk, or trick the Gangrel in question in any way. You're offering him a deal. Period. Nothing in what you said suggested you are trying to get him specifically to take it or make it sound attractive. You're just saying, &quot;here's the deal. Do you accept?&quot; And in that case, the Gangrel would decide based on the deal whether to accept or not.<br /> <br /> In a general sense, though, outside of your specific situation, rolling on social stuff is to give the players benefit of the doubt. It's the second resort, not first. First, you talk. If you make a great argument, it's probably convincing. No roll needed. I might raise an eyebrow if you have no Persuasion at all, and I might talk to you after the game about it if you consistently do that without any dots of Persuasion because the way they're playing isn't lining up with their abilities at all, which is an immersion issue. I'd almost certainly suggest rebuilding the character, mechanically, to reflect how it's actually being played.<br /> <br /> But mostly, if a player does awesome talking, I don't force a roll--that's just a chance for something to go stupidly wrong for no reason. That's a chance for a brilliant argument to get zero successes and, what, instead of saying what he literally just said, the character actually stumbled over his words and accidentally mentioned Hitler? No, that's bizarre and weird. A big one that sticks in my craw is intimidation. If someone makes a threat that is actually, legitimately scary, and the other guy has reason to believe it's true, why would I make them roll? Why can't the victim make the decision that he should indeed be scared of this guy? Why force it with a roll/give the roll a risk to fail?<br /> <br /> My go to example of this is threatening someone with a gun. Lets say you shot their buddy seconds ago right in front of them. Then, you hold the gun on them and say, simply, &quot;tell me what I want to know or I will shoot you.&quot; How could that fail? You're going to tell me there's a scenario where the guy looks at you and says, &quot;ha, you'e bluffing!&quot; No chance, no way. He's going to be scared and will need to make the choice: talk or get shot.<br /> <br /> To me, social rolls are failsafes. They're what happen when the player has no idea what to say or they say something really dumb or bad, but their character wouldn't be that bad at this. If someone makes a terrible argument, then, they get a roll for their character to fix the nonsense they just said. If someone has no clue what to say, while it would be my true and honest preference that their character is also tongue tied, the game is not solely for me, it is for everyone at the table, so, I give them a chance to roll and auto-pilot the argument. I always kind of hate that, but I accept it. My current group is one I &quot;rescued.&quot; I am trying to rehabilitate them and teach them how to actually roleplay after several years of only playing D&amp;D as a tactical combat game with some talking sometimes, so, I give them some breaks. When they're totally baffled as to what to say, they're fond of saying, &quot;I don't know to say. I press A. X successes.&quot; I know this sounds like I'm mocking them, but we talk about this openly all the time--it's their own words.<br /> <br /> And, for the record, I kind of don't love referring to this as the GM's fiat deciding what happens. To me, it's the GM's job to act as the NPC as accurately and with as much verisimilitude as possible. It should be readily apparent to anyone who knows a given NPC why they acted or responded the way they did. I strive for consistency here. The only reason the PCs won't already know how an NPC would react is if they don't know that NPC well or it has a hidden agenda or something, which, well, it means they have more information about them at least. So, yeah, it's not me, the GM, deciding what happens, it's the character responding appropriately to the situation that determines it, and I'm just trying to figure out what that response would be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853195#post853195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's actually only going to come up very rarely, then I withdraw my objection. I was thinking along the lines that it would be as common as Daeva feeding or Nosferatu interacting with people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but see, in my gaming paradigm, those things don't come up at all. Daeva generally just don't feed from the same person twice ever, and Nosferatu generally don't interact with humans in penalized ways. With this, the idea would be that Gangrel just avoid places or situations in which they might be confined against their will.<br /> <br /> But I am more than willing to go for an alternative idea to get them to appear wild, free, bestial, etc., by <i>avoiding</i> their clan bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  clarity 03-25-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T19:25:43-07:00","id":853280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853245#post853245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, in your specific example I would <i>especially</i> not roll anything, because you're not trying to convince, fast talk, or trick the Gangrel in question in any way. You're offering him a deal. Period. Nothing in what you said suggested you are trying to get him specifically to take it or make it sound attractive. You're just saying, &quot;here's the deal. Do you accept?&quot; And in that case, the Gangrel would decide based on the deal whether to accept or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's a nit-pick, honestly. It actually seems like we're on the same page. As long as the player said, &quot;I want to convince the Gangrel to take the deal, but don't know what to say, I press A.&quot; You'd let them make a social roll. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But mostly, if a player does awesome talking, I don't force a roll--that's just a chance for something to go stupidly wrong for no reason. That's a chance for a brilliant argument to get zero successes and, what, instead of saying what he literally just said, the character actually stumbled over his words and accidentally mentioned Hitler? No, that's bizarre and weird. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's a terrible example. I certainly wouldn't do that. But if a player made an impassioned plea, then I asked for a roll to see how well that plea was received and the dice came up nil, that means they failed to get what they want. I give them the option to take a beat for a dramatic failure, but otherwise the results don't come up with what they were hoping for.<br /> <br /> To equate that to mean I rewrite the scene to say the impassioned plea became a screed about Hitler is hyperbole. Plenty of impassioned pleas have fallen on deaf ears because of timing or circumstance. I'm certain I've seen con men movies where the guy is on a roll, makes the pitch, has everything in the bag, but then mentions a kid - and the target just so happens to have lost their kid, and so the con fails at the last second.<br /> <br /> My job as the ST is to figure out the product of these two mechanics:<br /> <br /> (Impassioned Roleplaying Plea) + (Zero Successes on the Dice) = (Plausible scenario of Failure)<br /> <br /> Being unable to see a plausible way to get to that product is a limitation of imagination, not a limitation of the system. That may sound meaner than I intend, but I think you're fully capable of coming up with non-hyperbolic ways of reconciling a good pitch with a bad roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A big one that sticks in my craw is intimidation. If someone makes a threat that is actually, legitimately scary, and the other guy has reason to believe it's true, why would I make them roll? Why can't the victim make the decision that he should indeed be scared of this guy? Why force it with a roll/give the roll a risk to fail? My go to example of this is threatening someone with a gun. Lets say you shot their buddy seconds ago right in front of them. Then, you hold the gun on them and say, simply, &quot;tell me what I want to know or I will shoot you.&quot; How could that fail? You're going to tell me there's a scenario where the guy looks at you and says, &quot;ha, you'e bluffing!&quot; No chance, no way. He's going to be scared and will need to make the choice: talk or get shot. </div> </div> </div>1) &quot;Fuck you, pull the trigger, you're going to kill me anyway.&quot;<br /> 2) &quot;I'll tell you what you want to know, just please don't hurt me! &lt;Plausible Lies&gt;&quot;<br /> <br /> Both are failed intimidation rolls. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, for the record, I kind of don't love referring to this as the GM's fiat deciding what happens. To me, it's the GM's job to act as the NPC as accurately and with as much verisimilitude as possible. It should be readily apparent to anyone who knows a given NPC why they acted or responded the way they did. I strive for consistency here. The only reason the PCs won't already know how an NPC would react is if they don't know that NPC well or it has a hidden agenda or something, which, well, it means they have more information about them at least. So, yeah, it's not me, the GM, deciding what happens, it's the character responding appropriately to the situation that determines it, and I'm just trying to figure out what that response would be. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this comes up sometimes. And I appreciate the idea that sometimes characters seem to write themselves, but they actually don't. You write them to the best of your ability, hopefully staying true to the character itself and breaking out of any preconceptions or limited perspectives that you bring to the table. But NPCs don't show up in a vacuum, even if it's a printed NPC that you're running, you're taking the guidelines and interpreting them.<br /> <br /> Fiat just means a declaration of authority, which is exactly what you are as an ST, the authority who controls the NPCs. It doesn't mean a declaration just because for no reason. <br /> <br /> I allow social mechanics at my table to influence important social situations. So do you, but as a backup. Otherwise, you determine the results to the best of your ability and ignore the dice. That's fine, and not a particularly uncommon approach, especially in 1E. But for me - who has experienced a wide range of player ability, and can run a table with both veterans and 'rescues' at the same 'top, I don't see a benefit to allowing my really persuasive friend to ignore social rolls any more than my martial arts friend getting to ignore grapple rolls. <br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks again for the discussion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T20:14:24-07:00","id":853300,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea:<br /> <br /> <i>The Gangrel are the Outsider, even to other Kindred. They are Wild. They are untamed.</i><br /> <br /> Clan Bane: A Gangrel in a city, town or crowd takes a -2 to all Social and Mental rolls (Except Streetwise and Intimidate) as they feel the yoke of civilisation clamping at their throats. Being in an area that is at least vaguely &quot;wild&quot; (such as a garden, park, zoo or the like) reduces the penalty to a -1. A Gangrel in his Haven or Feeding Grounds does not suffer the penalty at all (Storytellers may allow the lack of penalty to extend to whatever the Gangrel considers &quot;his territory&quot;). Furthermore, a Gangrel that feels an intense emotion must spend 1 Willpower or react impulsively, going with their gut instead of thinking things through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T22:07:13-07:00","id":853334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853280#post853280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that's a nit-pick, honestly. It actually seems like we're on the same page. As long as the player said, &quot;I want to convince the Gangrel to take the deal, but don't know what to say, I press A.&quot; You'd let them make a social roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if their intention was to convince him to take the deal, they could roll persuasion if they couldn't <i>actually</i> persuade him. Pushing A is just a joke...I don't require that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853280#post853280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being unable to see a plausible way to get to that product is a limitation of imagination, not a limitation of the system. That may sound meaner than I intend, but I think you're fully capable of coming up with non-hyperbolic ways of reconciling a good pitch with a bad roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I know. I love hyperbole, you got me. I could, I know, but I think that is actually unfairly punishing to people who have great ideas. It <i>can</i> discourage good roleplaying in people who are nervous or hesitant to talk normally, as the few times they speak up crash and burn anyway. I've seen it. Plus, I really enjoy seeing people get into it, being their character, coming up with great lines and ideas--I love it when players surprise me--so, I'd rather reward that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853280#post853280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) &quot;Fuck you, pull the trigger, you're going to kill me anyway.&quot;<br /> 2) &quot;I'll tell you what you want to know, just please don't hurt me! &lt;Plausible Lies&gt;&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>#1 is a thing only certain people would do...I don't think that would be a typical response. And those type of people, in my game, answer that way when they believe they will be killed anyway, not just because the intimidate failed. I kind of feel like that's a really weird way to take an intimidate failure, actually--it suggests that a successful roll is making someone believe you're a badass motherfucker who's willing to kill you over information, but also making them think you're <i>not </i>enough of a badass motherfucker that you'd kill them in the end no matter what? So, like, you're playing scary shuffleboard? A skilled scary person is trying to range find the right kind of scary and failing is being <i>too</i> scary sometimes? I...that doesn't connect for me.<br /> <br /> #2 is also strange to me. Are you suggesting people who are successfully intimidated can't lie? So...the being scary skill is also, like, shooting a magic curse that prevents lies? Or like, conveying how super good you are at lie detection so they don't try it? Yes, ok, hyperbole again, but, still, I find it weird that lying/not lying would be tied to how intimidating you are...why is that connected at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853280#post853280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for me - who has experienced a wide range of player ability, and can run a table with both veterans and 'rescues' at the same 'top, I don't see a benefit to allowing my really persuasive friend to ignore social rolls any more than my martial arts friend getting to ignore grapple rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we were in a LARP, I would agree. But, we're not. We're in a talking game, where literally 100% of the game takes place in a world build by our words. People who are good with words <i>should</i> do better at it, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> So, I'm not suggesting this is you because I don't know you well, but in my past experience discussing this issue, I've been faced with this exact argument many, many times before. Lots of roleplayers I've encountered want to argue that good speakers/fast talkers/highly social people should not get any advantage at all, and many of them mention that it's no different from a pro-athlete not getting an advantage on physical tasks. But, they never seem concerned about the people who are really smart getting an advantage. Knowing proper tactics and approaches has a huge impact on success in games, as does knowing how the rules interact, how to best build a character and spend their XP, etc. Just seems that roleplayers <i>tend</i> to be smarter than they are social, so, they are usually fine keeping their primary advantages in the game, but they fight tooth and nail to keep those social people's advantages out.<br /> <br /> To me, there's no physical component to playing the game, so, physical talent is meaningless to success. There is both a mental and a social component, though, and I have no problem allowing those talents to apply equally.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853280#post853280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, thanks again for the discussion!</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I also like these discussions for the most part. It's interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853300#post853300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea:<br /> <br /> <i>The Gangrel are the Outsider, even to other Kindred. They are Wild. They are untamed.</i><br /> <br /> Clan Bane: A Gangrel in a city, town or crowd takes a -2 to all Social and Mental rolls (Except Streetwise and Intimidate) as they feel the yoke of civilisation clamping at their throats. Being in an area that is at least vaguely &quot;wild&quot; (such as a garden, park, zoo or the like) reduces the penalty to a -1. A Gangrel in his Haven or Feeding Grounds does not suffer the penalty at all (Storytellers may allow the lack of penalty to extend to whatever the Gangrel considers &quot;his territory&quot;). Furthermore, a Gangrel that feels an intense emotion must spend 1 Willpower or react impulsively, going with their gut instead of thinking things through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do appreciate the idea, and the flavor you're suggesting, the &quot;Outsider,&quot; is cool and fitting. But your suggested flaw is really, super harsh. It basically prevents them from being in cities, like at all. Or it turns them into Nosferatu in the city at least. That's not really what I'm going for. My game's city is run by Gangrel, so, they have to be comfortable in a city. If I were starting a game from total scratch, I could consider that idea.<br /> <br /> It's also slightly out of line with the other Clan Banes, all of which are connected with Humanity. Keeping your Humanity higher helps mitigate every other Bane, while having a lower one exacerbates its problems. I'd like to keep some element of that in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  clarity 03-26-2016, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-25T22:17:35-07:00","id":853341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853334#post853334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do appreciate the idea, and the flavor you're suggesting, the &quot;Outsider&quot; is cool and fitting. But your suggested flaw is really, super harsh. It basically prevents them from being in cities, like at all. Or it turns them into Nosferatu in the city at least. That's not really what I'm going for. My game's city is run by Gangrel, so, they have to be comfortable in a city. If I were starting a game from total scratch, I could consider that idea.<br /> <br /> It's also slightly out of line with the other Clan Banes, all of which are connected with Humanity. Keeping your Humanity higher helps mitigate every other Bane, while having a lower one exacerbates its problems. I'd like to keep some element of that in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed the part where the Gangrel is exempt from the penalty in their Haven and Feeding Grounds, and the Storyteller can, if they find it appropriate (such as the case with a city that is entirely ruled by Gangrel) either lift or lessen the penalty because the Gangrel feels like he's in his territory? The bit about crowds can also be a tool for the Storyteller to reintroduce the Bane even in a city owned by Gangrel, to give them something to avoid behaviourally. Too many people at once can mean different things to each Gangrel. It can mean too many enemies, or too much prey, or it can become the metaphysical manifestation of humanity's choking influence over that which is Wild.<br /> <br /> If you want to keep the Humanity aspect in play, you can rework the penalty to 5 - half of their Humanity score (round down), which gives you a range from -0 at Humanity 10 to -5 at Humanity 1 and 0. Then, the &quot;lessened&quot; version from parks, gardens and the like is half the original penalty (round down again), so you get a spread between -0 at Humanity 10, 9 and 8, to -2 at Humanity 2, 1 and 0.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T05:28:21-07:00","id":853426,"title":"","content":"You mention &quot;successes&quot; - are you aware that unlike oWod, in majority of cases, one success is all your need for a full, real success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T08:33:26-07:00","id":853494,"title":"","content":"Okay. . . lots of things to say, having skimmed the replies since my last one.<br /> <br /> First, on the nature of predators. Fights to the death among animals are vanishingly rare, because it's just not survival-effective. &quot;Nature, red in tooth and claw&quot; is complete bunk. The paradigm for all animals is &quot;minimal effort for maximal reward.&quot; An animal that feels threatened will use a threat display to get the other animal to back down, because an actual fight is in no one's interest. Predators pretty much only kill so they can eat, because otherwise they're burning calories for no good purpose. As this relates to vampires (especially &quot;animalistic, primal&quot; Gangrel) is that, if simply Lashing Out with the Beast to establish dominance over someone would satisfy the Beast's desire, that's what they'll do. If their goal is to leave an area, and someone stands in their way, grabbing and biting and drinking all their blood is contrary to that goal; it's keeping them in the same place longer. They're far more likely to just shove the obstructing person aside and keep moving than to stop and engage in combat (which biting and drinking under time constraint pretty much inherently is.) Basically, unless their goal is explicitly or implicitly to kill someone, odds are vanishingly small that they'll actually do that. By which I mean, unless the goal of the frenzy is explicitly &quot;kill this person who humiliated/threatened/tried to kill me&quot; or implicitly fatal like &quot;drink until I'm full,&quot; vampires aren't going to use deliberately lethal force as a first resort. Now, Potence/Celerity/et al enhancements can easily make actions become fatal. If your goal is to escape the club, and the bouncer doesn't want to let you leave, and you bowl him aside with a Potence/Celerity 4 bull rush, tossing him 20 feet through the air to land on a table, that bouncer may well suffer fatal injuries. A vampire in frenzy may not expressly want to kill anyone who gets in his way, but he won't give a shit if he does, either.<br /> <br /> Next, on RP and rolls. If a player at my table wants to do something, but doesn't quite know how to go about it, I'll just let them roll normally. I encourage them to RP as much as possible, but if a player just can't come up with an impassioned plea or rousing speech off the top of their head, but their character has excellent ratings in the things that allow them to do that, I'm not going to punish them for it. They get to roll, and if the roll is good, they deliver, say, Mal's St. Crispin's Day speech from Serenity. If they roll poorly, they instead deliver ALL of Sheridan's MANY St. Crispin's Day speeches from Babylon 5, and the audience just tunes out after the first one. If the player does come up with a good speech, then I give them a bonus to the roll. A great example of this is the player in my game who played a Geist cop. She was a fantastic RPer, able to switch between &quot;good cop&quot; and &quot;bad cop&quot; at the drop of a hat, and managed to wring all kinds of information out of lowlife thugs really easily. I didn't always make her roll (especially if the information she was after was the only way of advancing the plot), but when I did, she did so at some hefty bonuses because her role-playing was so good.<br /> <br /> As for failures, people don't always know what they're made of until they're tested. In the example of a person who just watched their buddy get shot, then gets told they're next unless they talk, this random person could very well turn into a gibbering mess, or they could find a strength and courage they never even knew they had, look the shooter dead in the eye, and tell them to go fuck themselves. And either one, interestingly, could be the result of a failed Intimidation roll. A person could find the strength to face death with dignity, and withhold information from this very scary and dangerous person out of honor or spite, or they could be so terrified they can't remember their own name, nevermind whatever information the person is looking for.<br /> <br /> Next, the Bane itself. I'm less thinking mechanics at the moment than I am thematics. The idea of the fancy parties is still a sticking point for me. It's fine if you say that in your games vampires don't do that, but that's not going to hold true for all (or, I daresay, even most) games. Which means that your Bane would inherently only work for your group, or other groups very much like it. Which, if what you're looking for is help for a house rule for your table and no farther, is fine. But in that case, you need to explain more thoroughly what your game is like and what themes you're working with, so we don't start putting our own experiences on it that will not work for you. Also, the idea that &quot;rules the Gangrel themselves accepted&quot; was not made clear (at least, not to me.) Even so, it still feels like a Bane that can be abused by a jerkish ST or players by springing surprise clauses to rules the Gangrel in question had already accepted. Especially within Covenants like the Invictus or Ordo, where part of their, for lack of a better word, &quot;charm&quot; is the fact that as you rise higher in the organization, you learn more about how it works and have more obligations and responsibilities thrust upon you. Take the Ordo: &quot;Hey, join up with us, and we'll teach how to overcome all the weaknesses of being a vampire!&quot; Then the Gangrel actually signs up, and &quot;Okay, before we teach you anything, you have to apprentice for X amount of time as a Slave. Go do this for me.&quot; Once that's done, &quot;Okay, what do you want to learn? Oh, I can't actually teach you that. Go apprentice to this guy, he'll help you figure that out.&quot; And finally, &quot;Oh, no, we didn't mean ALL the vampire weakness, just some of them. Kind of. Well, not really.&quot; Granted, rules cannot accomodate all instances of the ST being an asshole, but they should at least try and minimize the opportunities asshole STs have to screw over their players. I can't help but think of one of the old Masquerade books I read, where the Baali were being described (perhaps for the first time), and a power they had to summon a greater demon from Hell, which had unconquerable stats. It was specifically noted that this power was intended to be used as a plot device (as in, the Baali are trying to summon a greater demon from Hell, we have to stop them before they succeed) and &quot;not as a means for sadistic Storytellers to waste the troupe&quot; (as in, the Baali summoned a greater demon from Hell, everyone dies.) The idea that Gangrel can find themselves in a more disdvantageous position than other vampires because someone decided to screw them over with fine print doesn't sit well with me, I think because it flies in the face of what I consider the Gangrel's greatest strength: adaptability. Their signature Discipline is basically about literally evolving to meet the needs of their new lives, the idea of Gangrel being rendered impotent by clever wordplay just bothers me. Basically, I don't feel it encourages Gangrel to act &quot;wild and free,&quot; because it doesn't prevent them from being trapped by the rules of Kindred society. The best they can do is tell the others &quot;fuck your rules&quot; and keep doing whatever they want, but they can still be &quot;trapped&quot; by them, forced to either obey the rule and suffer the effects of their Bane, or break the rule and suffer the consequences for that. Heads I win, tails you lose. Especially since the &quot;default&quot; setting of Requiem is pretty much all about &quot;how can I fuck over everyone else to my advantage within the law?&quot;<br /> <br /> I think, thematically, there's a lot more to Gangrel than &quot;Screw The Rules, I Have Claws!&quot; Perhaps, instead of penalizing them for acting within the stultifying structure of Kindred society, penalize them for doing so excessively. Gangrel can go to their Elysium parties and have legal discussions with Carthians and research the vampiric condition with the Ordo, but if they don't spend X amount of time on their own (or with their &quot;pack&quot; of fellows), they get some kind of penalty. This, I feel, encourages the &quot;wild and free&quot; stereotype of the Gangrel. Thematically, during a party or whatever, a Gangrel grows increasingly restless, until they finally say &quot;screw this, I'm outta here&quot; and go run naked in the woods or whatever it is they do. Other Kindred admit that it's rare to see a Gangrel at a social function unless they have to be there, rarer for them to stay any longer than absolutely necessary. It would also encourage players to make such social interactions as brief as possible, reinforcing the &quot;uncouth and direct&quot; stereotype of Gangrel. They don't go to a party, beat around the bush, chat up lots of people, and then finally get around to making small talk with the person they really need to see before, in a roundabout way, attempting to accomplish what they came to do. Instead, they'd walk right up to that person, say what they want, and then proceed to getting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:45:08-07:00","id":853567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853426#post853426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mention &quot;successes&quot; - are you aware that unlike oWod, in majority of cases, one success is all your need for a full, real success?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really?<br /> <br /> Yes, I know the rules of the game. The actual number of successes can be relevant in a variety of situations, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By which I mean, unless the goal of the frenzy is explicitly &quot;kill this person who humiliated/threatened/tried to kill me&quot; or implicitly fatal like &quot;drink until I'm full,&quot; vampires aren't going to use deliberately lethal force as a first resort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you skimmed over when we sorted this out. My assumption was that the frenzy would, indeed, be to punish the people in the examples.<br /> <br /> Everyone else, apparently, thought I was suggesting Gangrel would be terrified of corners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next, on RP and rolls. If a player at my table wants to do something, but doesn't quite know how to go about it, I'll just let them roll normally. I encourage them to RP as much as possible, but if a player just can't come up with an impassioned plea or rousing speech off the top of their head, but their character has excellent ratings in the things that allow them to do that, I'm not going to punish them for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, so we agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for failures, people don't always know what they're made of until they're tested. In the example of a person who just watched their buddy get shot, then gets told they're next unless they talk, this random person could very well turn into a gibbering mess, or they could find a strength and courage they never even knew they had, look the shooter dead in the eye, and tell them to go fuck themselves. And either one, interestingly, could be the result of a failed Intimidation roll. A person could find the strength to face death with dignity, and withhold information from this very scary and dangerous person out of honor or spite, or they could be so terrified they can't remember their own name, nevermind whatever information the person is looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't find that interesting, I find that...disconnected from the game world. When a character rolls intimidate, they are determining how intimidating they are. They are not determining what kind of person the guy they're intimidating is. <br /> <br /> This is crazy to me:<br /> <br /> PC: I got zero successes on my intimidate<br /> GM: The guy is so scared of you, he becomes a gibbering mess<br /> PC: But, I failed<br /> GM: Yeah, so, he doesn't talk, he just gibbers.<br /> PC: So, my intimidation skill is about...helping my prisoners talk coherently?<br /> <br /> Sorry, that just doesn't make sense. These skills should mean something and have predictable effects on the world. A PC's roll to determine how scary they are should not change the other guy's personality. If anything, those things should be the result of a successful or failed Resolve based roll of some kind on the NPC's part. The idea of failing an intimdate roll and then the other guy suddenly is too scared to talk, or succeeding and suddenly he can't lie, or any of the stuff the both of you have suggested here makes about as much sense to me as you asking a random passerby for help lifting something, and if you get an exceptional success on Persuasion, it turns out this guy is actually a ghoul with 5 Vigor and can easily lift anything you need.<br /> <br /> The mechanics and game world need to be connected in a logical way, or we won't enjoy the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next, the Bane itself. I'm less thinking mechanics at the moment than I am thematics. The idea of the fancy parties is still a sticking point for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, serious question: are most vampire games a series of fancy parties? Like, that's really a thing and not just a joke people use to make fun of vampire games? Because that just doesn't happen when I run games. Practically never.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even so, it still feels like a Bane that can be abused by a jerkish ST or players by springing surprise clauses to rules the Gangrel in question had already accepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I think using game rules to protect yourself from bad GMs is the wrong way to go. If you have a bad GM, stop playing with them. D&amp;D 3rd edition is what happens when you try to protect players from GMs with rules--it's a mess, and it ends up handicapping the good GMs far more than the protects you from the bad ones.<br /> <br /> Anyway, though, my intention is to houserule my own game, and if anyone else likes the idea, they can feel free to take it. But yeah, I'm actually still kind of amazed that a series of fancy parties is really how people run these things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that Gangrel can find themselves in a more disdvantageous position than other vampires because someone decided to screw them over with fine print doesn't sit well with me, I think because it flies in the face of what I consider the Gangrel's greatest strength: adaptability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's a cool theme. How do we work with that? Gangrel aren't the wild, bestial types, they're the adaptable ones? So, what would cause them trouble?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially since the &quot;default&quot; setting of Requiem is pretty much all about &quot;how can I fuck over everyone else to my advantage within the law?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>(in response to not just this, but everything in general about how vampire cities work) I think I really need to try and find a way to stomach all the purple prose nonsense and actually read some actual play posts around here. I'm not sure we're playing the same game at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853494#post853494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, thematically, there's a lot more to Gangrel than &quot;Screw The Rules, I Have Claws!&quot; Perhaps, instead of penalizing them for acting within the stultifying structure of Kindred society, penalize them for doing so excessively. Gangrel can go to their Elysium parties and have legal discussions with Carthians and research the vampiric condition with the Ordo, but if they don't spend X amount of time on their own (or with their &quot;pack&quot; of fellows), they get some kind of penalty. This, I feel, encourages the &quot;wild and free&quot; stereotype of the Gangrel. Thematically, during a party or whatever, a Gangrel grows increasingly restless, until they finally say &quot;screw this, I'm outta here&quot; and go run naked in the woods or whatever it is they do. Other Kindred admit that it's rare to see a Gangrel at a social function unless they have to be there, rarer for them to stay any longer than absolutely necessary. It would also encourage players to make such social interactions as brief as possible, reinforcing the &quot;uncouth and direct&quot; stereotype of Gangrel. They don't go to a party, beat around the bush, chat up lots of people, and then finally get around to making small talk with the person they really need to see before, in a roundabout way, attempting to accomplish what they came to do. Instead, they'd walk right up to that person, say what they want, and then proceed to getting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so, I love the concept. But how do you reflect that in a real flaw? Setting X amount of time is problematic in so many ways. For one, the game doesn't really track time in absolutes for the most part. Setting it as, &quot;every 2 scenes&quot; wouldn't work, because then the Gangrel has no reason to not make small talk and flit around the party (really, does this happen often?) as that's all one scene still. But make it &quot;2 hours&quot; instead is even worse. Then, the GM has to start tracking exact time and can no longer use &quot;Scene&quot; as the primary form of pacing. I am really interested in this concept, though. I like all of your thematic thoughts here, I just need to actually mechanize them somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:08:38-07:00","id":853609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't find that interesting, I find that...disconnected from the game world. When a character rolls intimidate, they are determining how intimidating they are. They are not determining what kind of person the guy they're intimidating is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is the disconnect. 2E is agenda based, not action based.<br /> <br /> Not,<br /> <br /> PC: &quot;I roll to see how intimidating I am.&quot;<br /> <br /> Rather,<br /> <br /> PC: &quot;I want to get information out of him.&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;How?&quot;<br /> PC: &quot;By Intimidating him. Also, I shoot his partner first. Does that give me a bonus?&quot;<br /> ST: &quot;Hell yes. Gonna be a humanity check also, but definitely a bonus.&quot;<br /> <br /> The agenda is specifically <i>getting the information</i>. The player has a number of ways (actions) to do that. Trick him. Persuade him. Seduce him. Blackmail him. Intimidate him. Torture him. <br /> <br /> <b>The action is second to the agenda.</b> <br /> <br /> Again, look at all the new per-your-definition 'story-mechanics' - even combat, with the beaten down and agenda based system is moving that way. 2E is infused with it. Hence my initial suggestion that you may be better off starting with 1E, and pulling over the systems you do like (Combat, Disciplines, the other crunchy systems). Rather than start with 2E and try and unweave the as-you-say story-mechanics from everything. <br /> <br /> And let me re-iterate, none of this is an indictment on your playstyle. I myself have had really great and fun games run very similar to everything you do, and even <i>run </i>games that are similar in the past. I just would never run that kind of a game using the 2E rules. And I hit this dilemma directly when thinking about a 2E LARP. A lot of the concepts don't translate easily (Though to be fair David Hill did post some cool discipline conversions for a potential LARP), but it's going to be an intensive project to convert the whole thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is crazy to me:<br /> <br /> PC: I got zero successes on my intimidate<br /> GM: The guy is so scared of you, he becomes a gibbering mess<br /> PC: But, I failed<br /> GM: Yeah, so, he doesn't talk, he just gibbers.<br /> PC: So, my intimidation skill is about...helping my prisoners talk coherently?<br /> <br /> Sorry, that just doesn't make sense. These skills should mean something and have predictable effects on the world. A PC's roll to determine how scary they are should not change the other guy's personality. If anything, those things should be the result of a successful or failed Resolve based roll of some kind on the NPC's part. The idea of failing an intimdate roll and then the other guy suddenly is too scared to talk, or succeeding and suddenly he can't lie, or any of the stuff the both of you have suggested here makes about as much sense to me as you asking a random passerby for help lifting something, and if you get an exceptional success on Persuasion, it turns out this guy is actually a ghoul with 5 Vigor and can easily lift anything you need.<br /> <br /> The mechanics and game world need to be connected in a logical way, or we won't enjoy the game. </div> </div> </div>Hopefully my description above re: agenda-based vs. action-based play helped clarify this. And again, there is nothing wrong with not liking agenda-based play, or director/writer-style play at all. It just seems like you really want to believe 2E isn't what I would define as agenda-based (if other lurkers have a better term for what I'm trying to explain, please hop in). I think I, and a lot of people who have sort of posted counter to your ideas, are seeing that agenda-based style as integral to the system. And in fact, find it one of the more compelling aspects of the system.<br /> <br /> Beats, Aspirations, Breaking Points, Touchstones, Social Rolls, Dramatic Failures - It's difficult for me to see much of a 2E game when you strip all those things out. <br /> <br /> But, moving forward - that's what you want to do, and that's great too. I would just say be prepared to have this conversation a lot, 'cause I really think you're swimming upstream against a lot of the 2E current. <br /> <br /> For example, maybe a better question would have been, &quot;I'm running 1E, but I want the Clan Flaws to match the new 2E versions. Here's my ones for the first four clans. But I'm having trouble with the Gangrel. Any ideas?&quot; Instead of, &quot;Hey I want to change the Gangrel Flaw in my 2E game, but I don't want it to have anything to do with beats, aspirations, breaking points, touchstones, social rolls, dramatic failures, frenzy or any other agenda-style play.&quot; : )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T12:44:39-07:00","id":853621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you skimmed over when we sorted this out. My assumption was that the frenzy would, indeed, be to punish the people in the examples.<br /> <br /> Everyone else, apparently, thought I was suggesting Gangrel would be terrified of corners.</div> </div> </div> </div>That image makes me laugh <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously, though, I just wanted to clarify my take on what frenzy is and means. Looks like things did get fairly well hashed out, just wanted to put in my further two cents, especially as regards the animal analogies. Call it ego if you like <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, so we agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't find that interesting, I find that...disconnected from the game world. When a character rolls intimidate, they are determining how intimidating they are. They are not determining what kind of person the guy they're intimidating is.<br /> <br /> This is crazy to me:<br /> <br /> PC: I got zero successes on my intimidate<br /> GM: The guy is so scared of you, he becomes a gibbering mess<br /> PC: But, I failed<br /> GM: Yeah, so, he doesn't talk, he just gibbers.<br /> PC: So, my intimidation skill is about...helping my prisoners talk coherently?<br /> <br /> Sorry, that just doesn't make sense. These skills should mean something and have predictable effects on the world. A PC's roll to determine how scary they are should not change the other guy's personality. If anything, those things should be the result of a successful or failed Resolve based roll of some kind on the NPC's part. The idea of failing an intimdate roll and then the other guy suddenly is too scared to talk, or succeeding and suddenly he can't lie, or any of the stuff the both of you have suggested here makes about as much sense to me as you asking a random passerby for help lifting something, and if you get an exceptional success on Persuasion, it turns out this guy is actually a ghoul with 5 Vigor and can easily lift anything you need.<br /> <br /> The mechanics and game world need to be connected in a logical way, or we won't enjoy the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the thing is, skills never auto-succeed. Putting a gun in someone's hand does not give them infinite Intimidate dice. A pump-action shotgun, when racked, adds +1 to Intimidate checks because, as Gabriel Iglesias puts, &quot;when I hear <i>chik-chak</i>, the joke is <b>over</b>.&quot; If there's any chance that the action might fail (such as when someone else is opposing you, as Intimidate does by default), you have to roll. And if you fail, you don't successfully intimidate the target into doing what you want. It's actually very easy to scare someone so much that they can't tell you what you want, even if they dearly want to. That's where there's a &quot;good cop&quot; in the classic &quot;good cop, bad cop.&quot; And we're not talking fundamental changes in a person's personality here. We're talking how, in this instance, a hypothetical person with a gun to the head of another hypothetical person and the obvious willingness to use it might still fail an Indimidate check, and how that result might be described in that particular instance. The target of Intimidate doesn't suddenly gain bunches of Willpower, representing that they now know they're made of way sterner stuff than they ever suspected, they just found, in that moment, the courage to hold to their convictions in the face of certain, terrifying death (though a player who found their character in such a situation, and passed such a loaded against them Intimidate roll, I would easily allow to spend Experiences on Willpower, Resolve, and/or Composure, precisely because of that.) The dice inform the story and vice versa, failing a roll can add to the drama as effectively as succeeding, and saying that a roll can't fail (or succeed) in a given circumstance due to modifiers (essentially what you're talking about) undercuts the roll one plays in constructing the other.<br /> <br /> For this hypothetical Intimidate roll, I'd add a capped bonus of +5 (if I recall, miscellaneous bonuses to rolls still can't exceed five dice in 2E). Between the gun and the obvious willingness to use it, the Intimidating character is about as scary as they can possibly be. But the roll can still fail. In which case, it's my job as ST to determine why that happened. Maybe the other person believes that the Intimidator isn't actually willing to kill them, because they can't get answers from a corpse? Maybe they do find that ability to spit in the face of iminent death. Maybe they're so terrified they can't answer. Whatever works best for the NPC in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, serious question: are most vampire games a series of fancy parties? Like, that's really a thing and not just a joke people use to make fun of vampire games? Because that just doesn't happen when I run games. Practically never.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, politics and social interaction are major themes of the game as written. It can be as played up or ignored as individual Chronicles and troupes like, but it is an inherent part of the Requiem. I can only speak to my games personally, so I'll drop a little background: My chronicle (on indefinite hiatus, sadly) centers around three cities, only two of which the players actually got to visit before we broke. In the Twin Cities, St. Paul and some suburbs are controlled by the Invictus, while Minneapolis and some suburbs are controlled by the Carthians, and the two Covenants are essentially in a cold war. Getting anything done invariably involves currying favor with one group or the other, who of course want things done for them in return. Gotham City, my place for Lovecraftian horror, is controlled by Mafia-styled Invictus, with a Carthian rebel movement trying to kick them out. The players didn't really get a chance to explore the eldritch horror elements, though, instead being caught up in more politics. Now, some of this is in response to my Masquerade game, where I was a much less subtle Storyteller, and the plot was mostly &quot;here's the bad guy, go kick his ass.&quot; My players seem to enjoy the switch, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general, I think using game rules to protect yourself from bad GMs is the wrong way to go. If you have a bad GM, stop playing with them. D&amp;D 3rd edition is what happens when you try to protect players from GMs with rules--it's a mess, and it ends up handicapping the good GMs far more than the protects you from the bad ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually liked 3.5 compared to 3rd, though yeah, when the group I was in at the time upgraded, it felt like the devs had been sitting at our table, looking at everything the munchkin gamer had been doing, and taking steps to minimize it. My point is, though, that while you can't make rules jerkass-proof, they should be less obviously easy to exploit. At least make the jerks work for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, though, my intention is to houserule my own game, and if anyone else likes the idea, they can feel free to take it. But yeah, I'm actually still kind of amazed that a series of fancy parties is really how people run these things.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's certainly more to it than that, but interacting with other vampires in social situations is a part of it. It doesn't have to be the stereotypical art gallery cheese and whine session, but whatever group holds power is going to make such gatherings fit their ideas of what are comfortable, and make everyone else uncomfortable (so they have the advantage.) My Minneapolis Carthians meet in a kind of democratic council, with representatives from the other supernatural &quot;races&quot; present, to make sure that things run as smoothly as possible for everyone. The Ordo, Circle, and Sanctum representatives on that council are basically the people who had nothing better to do in their respective Covenants, so nothing's really being lost by having them attend yet another Carthian meeting. The Invictus meetings (not that my players have been to one, so I haven't really fleshed them out) are more likely &quot;King and his Court&quot; type affairs, where only the &quot;important&quot; people get announced, and anyone with a petition has to wait on line to be heard, and it may take them quite awhile to get to you. All to remind you where the real power lies, you insolent peasant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, that's a cool theme. How do we work with that? Gangrel aren't the wild, bestial types, they're the adaptable ones? So, what would cause them trouble?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being bored?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(in response to not just this, but everything in general about how vampire cities work) I think I really need to try and find a way to stomach all the purple prose nonsense and actually read some actual play posts around here. I'm not sure we're playing the same game at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which, again, is fine. Just bear in mind that a lot of objections will be &quot;that won't work at all in my game&quot; because everyone's games are different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853567#post853567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so, I love the concept. But how do you reflect that in a real flaw? Setting X amount of time is problematic in so many ways. For one, the game doesn't really track time in absolutes for the most part. Setting it as, &quot;every 2 scenes&quot; wouldn't work, because then the Gangrel has no reason to not make small talk and flit around the party (really, does this happen often?) as that's all one scene still. But make it &quot;2 hours&quot; instead is even worse. Then, the GM has to start tracking exact time and can no longer use &quot;Scene&quot; as the primary form of pacing. I am really interested in this concept, though. I like all of your thematic thoughts here, I just need to actually mechanize them somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is kind of the sticky widget. First, I'd establish the thematic element that, even when the Bane isn't mechancially enforced, thematically, a Gangrel always chaffes in social situations, because they'd rather be off doing something actually productive (or just more fun.) Second, I'd tie it with Humanity, since like you said, the Bane all involve Humanity in some way. Maybe making it a certain number of rolls in a social situation based on Humanity? Equal to Humanity, or Humanity x2, or x1.5, whatever works best. So if they waste time rolling in verbal sparring matches with the Daeva, they might not have the dice pools they want when they go to ask the Prince for a favor. Maybe limit it to social rolls, or expand it to any kind of roll. For instance, if trying to conceal a weapon or document or whatever before going into the party, the Gangrel is thinking &quot;I'm wasting my time on this, I'd rather be out hunting.&quot; Thus, that counts as one of their &quot;free&quot; &quot;party&quot; rolls they get to make before whatever penalty there is starts kicking in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T17:22:19-07:00","id":853756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, this is the disconnect. 2E is agenda based, not action based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so, I think what you mean is, &quot;the people on this forum mostly use 2E as if it were agenda based.&quot; Nothing in the rules inherently makes it that. Nothing I've seen at least. It looks pretty open ended as to whether you treat it as task based (as I do) or &quot;agenda based.&quot; The only thing that appears explicitly agenda based is the Beaten Down condition, which I kind of like, but the party despises.<br /> <br /> Agenda based is an odd choice of wording, but I understand. In general, I see the opposite of Task based resolution as Conflict based resolution. The idea is basically, you don't roll to take an action, you roll to accomplish a goal. Now, I don't like conflict based resolution because the specific action you take generally doesn't matter. There are no short cuts or better choices, just throw your pool of dice at the difficulty and then figure out what happens. I think its impossible to treat Requiem that way, so, I think you're proposing, like, a hybrid, maybe. You're still suggesting you roll to solve a conflict, but the method you're using to solve it, at the least, affects the pools involved. I get it. I don't like it, but I get what you're saying. I just don't think that's the <i>only </i>way to run the game, nor do I think it's even necessarily the default. I don't think the book specifies one way or the other. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The agenda is specifically <i>getting the information</i>. The player has a number of ways (actions) to do that. Trick him. Persuade him. Seduce him. Blackmail him. Intimidate him. Torture him.<br /> <br /> <b>The action is second to the agenda.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but to me, I think you understand, that is not the case. You take actions, and the results of those actions accomplish your goal. Well, hopefully. There are times when you might successfully take an action and the result is totally different than you expected, but if you're paying attention and the GM is doing things right, those things times should be rare, and mostly due to hidden information. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, look at all the new per-your-definition 'story-mechanics' - even combat, with the beaten down and agenda based system is moving that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of think the Beaten Down condition is just about the only way it's written into the system. And even that, I kind of mostly feel like it's GM hand holding to help them realize people don't fight to the death, or to force PCs to realize, &quot;hey, don't fight to the death, moron, you're not a murder hobo.&quot; It has uses, for sure, but it doesn't require &quot;agenda based&quot; gameplay beyond, &quot;are you trying to kill this guy or not?&quot; The party rebelled pretty hard when it first came up, though, so, I stopped using it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2E is infused with it. Hence my initial suggestion that you may be better off starting with 1E, and pulling over the systems you do like (Combat, Disciplines, the other crunchy systems). Rather than start with 2E and try and unweave the as-you-say story-mechanics from everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a perspective thing. To me, I'm leaving out a few minor things, and explaining that I'm using, basically all of the rules that matter to me and my game from 2e is way more complicated than &quot;yeah, I play 2e with these little things swept under the rug.&quot; But to you, those things aren't little, apparently, they're huge, big deals, that drive the whole playing experience for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just seems like you really want to believe 2E isn't what I would define as agenda-based (if other lurkers have a better term for what I'm trying to explain, please hop in). I think I, and a lot of people who have sort of posted counter to your ideas, are seeing that agenda-based style as integral to the system. And in fact, find it one of the more compelling aspects of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not believe it is integral to the system, I just think it allows for both and you guys just use it differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beats, Aspirations, Breaking Points, Touchstones, Social Rolls, Dramatic Failures - It's difficult for me to see much of a 2E game when you strip all those things out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely use Breaking Points. I use social rolls (just not the same way you use them, evidently). Dramatic Failures happen when you roll 1 on a chance die, and it's happened three times so far in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, moving forward - that's what you want to do, and that's great too. I would just say be prepared to have this conversation a lot, 'cause I really think you're swimming upstream against a lot of the 2E current.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I guess I never saw WoD as a story game before, because it really wasn't, and it surprised me to find out that, &quot;Oh, I guess it really is now.&quot; I'm fine with having the conversation a lot, though. It's interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853609#post853609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, maybe a better question would have been, &quot;I'm running 1E, but I want the Clan Flaws to match the new 2E versions. Here's my ones for the first four clans. But I'm having trouble with the Gangrel. Any ideas?&quot; Instead of, &quot;Hey I want to change the Gangrel Flaw in my 2E game, but I don't want it to have anything to do with beats, aspirations, breaking points, touchstones, social rolls, dramatic failures, frenzy or any other agenda-style play.&quot; : )</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, that would be totally off, though. All of those discipline changes, combat rather than murder....just so much of everything is different. Maybe, 2e rules with 1e attitude? I don't know.<br /> <br /> I'm going to be honest here about another houserule thing I do. I actually do change the 1-4 successes and only 5+ is different thing. I never liked that in 1e. I pay attention to the number of successes they roll and it always impacts it. 1 success is a &quot;complete&quot; success for the action they're taking, but more successes matter and make it even better. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thing is, skills never auto-succeed. Putting a gun in someone's hand does not give them infinite Intimidate dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But Intimidate, to me, is the skill that lets you appear scary, that lets you scare people without needing the means to back it up. I don't see it as mind control, though. Someone has the right to be scared of something without the other person being successful. In real life, if I was being held at gun point, I would be afraid of that guy with the gun. Period. I am. I don't care how shaky his hands are, how incoherent his threats are, he has a gun, and a gun could kill me. There is no circumstance where that guy asks me a question and I defy him. Zero. <br /> <br /> I don't consider it an auto-success, I consider it a logical conclusion drawn by the victim. If you have a gun and they have reason to believe you will use it on them (especially if they just saw you do so), they have the right to preserve themselves without requiring that person to successfully be scary. Their actions were already scary. No need for any pretense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pump-action shotgun, when racked, adds +1 to Intimidate checks</div> </div> </div> </div>If you know nothing about guns, because either you just ejected a perfectly good shell, or you were dumb enough not to have your shotgun ready to fire in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's actually very easy to scare someone so much that they can't tell you what you want, even if they dearly want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. But I would not consider that a function of <i>failing</i> an intimidate roll. Scaring someone too much means you <i>super scary</i>. That's the function of a <i>super successful</i> intimidate roll. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, politics and social interaction are major themes of the game as written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I'm not talking about lacking politics and social stuff, I'm specifically referring to fancy parties. I feel like a lot of the trappings of vampire society that started with Masquerade way back in the early '90s is a product of, well, the '80s. That was the era when corporations and high society first became bad guys and media started showing us the slick black tie events these modern predators walked in. But, that stuff isn't really a thing anymore. The image is different. Rich people are less scary and more, I don't know, absurd. They're still the bad guys, but their spoiled, out of touch, and helpless when they can't throw money at the problem, since they were just given everything in life. They're not the monsters anymore, so, it doesn't feel as impactful to keep reiterating that scene in Vampire games. The vampires in power are going to be more than a hundred years old and the every day ones are going to be from the last 20 years mostly. You're lucky to even deal with a handful of vampires with that '80s mentality.<br /> <br /> So, my Vancouver is run by Jack Deighton, the actual real founder of Vancouver who, in my world, became a vampire. He and his Gangrel bloodline have an iron grip on the city. They have a few events, which feel like informal hang outs at a saloon where the Prince mostly just tells stories and everyone drinks (blood from drunk people), reflecting both the original culture of Mr. Deighton and the modern hipster culture. There are remnants of the covenants around, but they barely matter.<br /> <br /> My Twin Cities are run by, basically two groups of Viking vampires trying to win favor from the Crone's Cult of Thor. It's a lot more complicated and nuanced, I could tell you about it some time if you're interested, but it's still not fancy parties, it's old school mead hall shit.<br /> <br /> My Phoenix is run by a Carthian congress, with representatives drawn from political parties who maintain a certain baseline membership. Werewolves are integrated into society, but tensions flare because the Ordo Dracul that were ousted to allow the Carthians control have figured out how to use the Carthian democratic system against them. They start stirring the shit and putting the Carthians and Werewolves at odds with each other, fracturing the alliance and hoping to snatch up power when it finally crumbles. This setting had the closest thing to formal parties, but, it was still mostly just informal and never &quot;everyone is there at once.&quot;<br /> <br /> My LA is run by Carthians who foolishly chose not to restrict making children--they thought people were more responsible than they are and strove to create a city of ultimate freedom. A massive overpopulation of vampires floods the city and the vamps know almost nothing. Vampire teenagers still live with their parents, possibly not even really understanding their condition. It's crazy. They have a two consul system in place, like ancient Rome, but all of these clueless new vampires get a vote in this extreme democratic paradise, so, when the populace elects a local punk rock star that was embraced literally yesterday as consul, things start to fall apart. The Roman senate like structure in place falls apart when one of the consuls turns Elysium into a concert... <br /> <br /> There are many others. I don't know, I guess I don't run any city in a &quot;typical&quot; fashion where all five covenants exist with a Prince that throws fancy parties and people curry whispered favors in tuxes and ball gowns.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotham City, my place for Lovecraftian horror, is controlled by Mafia-styled Invictus, with a Carthian rebel movement trying to kick them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bizarre, tangential question: where is your Gotham City? Is it anywhere near those twin cities? Do you act like it's just New York like most people do? Or do you put where the official DC continuity does, in New Jersey, where it's kind of an Atlantic City stand in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually liked 3.5 compared to 3rd</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually meant 3rd edition in general, not 3.5 specifically. AD&amp;D 2e was written basically giving the PCs very little information. Like, you didn't even know your saves. Those were in the DMG. 3rd edition was a radical swing in the opposite direction, giving players all the rules and designing everything so that players and GMs played with the exact same tools, attempting to prevent GMs from screwing the players and hoarding information, powers, etc. 3rd is still a good game, but all the places it falls down are where it was trying to protect players from their GMs instead of just trusting that that the GM would be playing in good faith. I just think the GM's job is to make sure the players are having a good time. GM vs. PCs is not a mindset I can get behind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's certainly more to it than that, but interacting with other vampires in social situations is a part of it. It doesn't have to be the stereotypical art gallery cheese and whine session, but whatever group holds power is going to make such gatherings fit their ideas of what are comfortable, and make everyone else uncomfortable (so they have the advantage.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, ok, they're not all fancy parties, yeah? That makes more sense. But also, when you're trying to restrict their power, why invite everyone else anyway? Why have public parties all the time? What's the point? Businesses are run in the board room, not the charity gala. I feel like that concept in general is an artificial thing invented so that GMs can show off the super powerful political players to the PCs. <br /> <br /> Most business in my cities is conducted during small meetings or over the phone or something, not during grand affairs that every vampire goes to. Those basically never happen. Even Elysium is usually something many (maybe even most) vampires ignore or avoid. Grand affairs are <i>obviously</i> just an excuse for the ones in charge to throw their weight around and show everyone else their place, so, why would the ones under their thumb bother? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Minneapolis Carthians meet in a kind of democratic council, with representatives from the other supernatural &quot;races&quot; present, to make sure that things run as smoothly as possible for everyone. The Ordo, Circle, and Sanctum representatives on that council are basically the people who had nothing better to do in their respective Covenants, so nothing's really being lost by having them attend yet another Carthian meeting.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that sounds right to me. Not a fancy party.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Invictus meetings (not that my players have been to one, so I haven't really fleshed them out) are more likely &quot;King and his Court&quot; type affairs, where only the &quot;important&quot; people get announced, and anyone with a petition has to wait on line to be heard, and it may take them quite awhile to get to you. All to remind you where the real power lies, you insolent peasant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, though, sounds less like something a real vampire would actually want or do and more like something a crazy old guy guy who lived during &quot;King and his Court&quot; time would impose on people because nobody else could possible beat him in a test of power. In other words, for Masquerade, where those insane, un-topple-able power structures were obnoxious and stifling for players. They literally couldn't advance. Ever. Because they couldn't ever match that guy's generation or his thousand years of experience. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being bored?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, how to mechanize that?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853621#post853621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is kind of the sticky widget. First, I'd establish the thematic element that, even when the Bane isn't mechancially enforced, thematically, a Gangrel always chaffes in social situations, because they'd rather be off doing something actually productive (or just more fun.) Second, I'd tie it with Humanity, since like you said, the Bane all involve Humanity in some way. Maybe making it a certain number of rolls in a social situation based on Humanity? Equal to Humanity, or Humanity x2, or x1.5, whatever works best. So if they waste time rolling in verbal sparring matches with the Daeva, they might not have the dice pools they want when they go to ask the Prince for a favor. Maybe limit it to social rolls, or expand it to any kind of roll. For instance, if trying to conceal a weapon or document or whatever before going into the party, the Gangrel is thinking &quot;I'm wasting my time on this, I'd rather be out hunting.&quot; Thus, that counts as one of their &quot;free&quot; &quot;party&quot; rolls they get to make before whatever penalty there is starts kicking in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, for me, this is going to run into issues. I suspect I call for many fewer rolls than others do, and when something does call for rolls, I probably use way more, because I resolve things by task, so each individual piece gets a roll, rather than resolving the conflict in one go. Number of rolls is also just so variable...it seems like it will either never happen or always happen, and it'll really just be the flavor text stuff making Gangrel feel like they ought to. I don't know, I'll consider it. I do like the direction, though, still, just having trouble with the execution.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T18:18:01-07:00","id":853779,"title":"","content":"I'd like to chime in to point out that rolling Intimidation is not determining how intimidating you are. It's determining whether or not you succeed at intimidating someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T18:38:23-07:00","id":853792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I guess I never saw WoD as a story game before, because it really wasn't, and it surprised me to find out that, &quot;Oh, I guess it really is now.&quot; I'm fine with having the conversation a lot, though. It's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought WoD (even as far back as VtM) was more story-focused than anything else. You <i>could</i> play it like D&amp;D (kick down the door, kill the &quot;monsters,&quot; take their stuff so you can kick in a bigger door and kill bigger monsters), but that wasn't the way it was designed to be played. Curious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. But Intimidate, to me, is the skill that lets you appear scary, that lets you scare people without needing the means to back it up. I don't see it as mind control, though. Someone has the right to be scared of something without the other person being successful. In real life, if I was being held at gun point, I would be afraid of that guy with the gun. Period. I am. I don't care how shaky his hands are, how incoherent his threats are, he has a gun, and a gun could kill me. There is no circumstance where that guy asks me a question and I defy him. Zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, and I think there's way more to it than that. Intimidate is about manipulating someone to do what you want through fear. It's not just about being scary, it's about using that scariness to achieve a desired outcome. Failing the roll doesn't necessarily mean you failed to be scary, it means you failed to properly utilize that scariness to achieve your desired outcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't consider it an auto-success, I consider it a logical conclusion drawn by the victim. If you have a gun and they have reason to believe you will use it on them (especially if they just saw you do so), they have the right to preserve themselves without requiring that person to successfully be scary. Their actions were already scary. No need for any pretense.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you also seem to be saying that a person with a gun to someone else's head and a clear willingness to use it automatically succeeds at Intimidate checks. That seems wrong to me, somehow. If that's not what you mean, then I apologize for continued derailment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you know nothing about guns, because either you just ejected a perfectly good shell, or you were dumb enough not to have your shotgun ready to fire in the first place. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe, yeah, there is that. Still, even though I intellectually know that, I daresay that the sound of a racking shotgun is ingrained enough my hindbrain as a &quot;bad sound&quot; that it would probably make me a bit more scared. I think I even saw a show talking about police officers and firearms where a cop stated that racking a shotgun, loaded or not, is a great way to get a lot of perps to stop and throw their hands in the air. But, I'm just quoting the rule from the books (may have only been in 1E, not sure.) Hilariously, the Geist Cop in my game actually did that on an Intimidate check and failed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. But I would not consider that a function of <i>failing</i> an intimidate roll. Scaring someone too much means you <i>super scary</i>. That's the function of a <i>super successful</i> intimidate roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, are you saying that you can still fail at the goal you set for yourself with a roll even if you succeeded a lot?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. I'm not talking about lacking politics and social stuff, I'm specifically referring to fancy parties. I feel like a lot of the trappings of vampire society that started with Masquerade way back in the early '90s is a product of, well, the '80s. That was the era when corporations and high society first became bad guys and media started showing us the slick black tie events these modern predators walked in. But, that stuff isn't really a thing anymore. The image is different. Rich people are less scary and more, I don't know, absurd. They're still the bad guys, but their spoiled, out of touch, and helpless when they can't throw money at the problem, since they were just given everything in life. They're not the monsters anymore, so, it doesn't feel as impactful to keep reiterating that scene in Vampire games. The vampires in power are going to be more than a hundred years old and the every day ones are going to be from the last 20 years mostly. You're lucky to even deal with a handful of vampires with that '80s mentality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I think the &quot;rich people are bad guys&quot; trope is still alive and well in the modern day, precisely because they're so out-of-touch with the experiences of most people, and are still doing everything they can to build on what they have at the expense of &quot;the lower orders.&quot; I don't want to get into a really loaded discussion here, so let's just say that there's a certain rich person prominently in the news right now who resembles this to a tee, and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, my Vancouver is run by Jack Deighton, the actual real founder of Vancouver who, in my world, became a vampire. He and his Gangrel bloodline have an iron grip on the city. They have a few events, which feel like informal hang outs at a saloon where the Prince mostly just tells stories and everyone drinks (blood from drunk people), reflecting both the original culture of Mr. Deighton and the modern hipster culture. There are remnants of the covenants around, but they barely matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Twin Cities are run by, basically two groups of Viking vampires trying to win favor from the Crone's Cult of Thor. It's a lot more complicated and nuanced, I could tell you about it some time if you're interested, but it's still not fancy parties, it's old school mead hall shit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds awesome, and I'd definitely like to hear more!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bizarre, tangential question: where is your Gotham City? Is it anywhere near those twin cities? Do you act like it's just New York like most people do? Or do you put where the official DC continuity does, in New Jersey, where it's kind of an Atlantic City stand in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I put it in New Jersey, feeling that it felt right as a &quot;dark counterpart to New York.&quot; I also borrowed a little more from the Batman continuity than a I probably should have (to the point where the Mage Consilium is run by Bruce Wayne, who is NOT Batman, but is a Mastigos with a Bat-flavored Nimbus, and most of the other Councilors are based on and named for Batman characters. The head of the Mysterium, for example, has the Shadow Name Aptenodytes.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually meant 3rd edition in general, not 3.5 specifically. AD&amp;D 2e was written basically giving the PCs very little information. Like, you didn't even know your saves. Those were in the DMG. 3rd edition was a radical swing in the opposite direction, giving players all the rules and designing everything so that players and GMs played with the exact same tools, attempting to prevent GMs from screwing the players and hoarding information, powers, etc. 3rd is still a good game, but all the places it falls down are where it was trying to protect players from their GMs instead of just trusting that that the GM would be playing in good faith. I just think the GM's job is to make sure the players are having a good time. GM vs. PCs is not a mindset I can get behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely agree with you there. Unless you're playing a game where that is the point and part of the fun, and everyone's OK with it (Call of Cthulhu or Paranoia, or somesuch), the GM and players should be working together to create a story, not seeing if the GM can waste the PCs before the PCs can <a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/The_Henderson_Scale_of_Plot_Derailment\" target=\"_blank\">2.5 Henderson</a> the GM's plot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, ok, they're not all fancy parties, yeah? That makes more sense. But also, when you're trying to restrict their power, why invite everyone else anyway? Why have public parties all the time? What's the point? Businesses are run in the board room, not the charity gala. I feel like that concept in general is an artificial thing invented so that GMs can show off the super powerful political players to the PCs.<br /> <br /> Most business in my cities is conducted during small meetings or over the phone or something, not during grand affairs that every vampire goes to. Those basically never happen. Even Elysium is usually something many (maybe even most) vampires ignore or avoid. Grand affairs are <i>obviously</i> just an excuse for the ones in charge to throw their weight around and show everyone else their place, so, why would the ones under their thumb bother?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's less about getting business done (though that can certainly happen), but it's really the only place Kindred can meaningfully interact with each other. Humans are social creatures (for the most part), and we crave, even require, social interaction. Vampires may be living corpses, but they still have that fundamental need. So they gather together to they can talk to someone, anyone, with whom they have some vague shared (un)life experience. Of course, the fact that they're undead bloodsucking corpses with a demonic ragemonster inside them means that whenever more than one of them is in the same room, they start trying to dick each other over, but that's another matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, that sounds right to me. Not a fancy party.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but still a social event where the rules and protocols must be observed. In a situation like this, the Bane you were thinking of could be abused by jerkish STs (or even other players) by pointing out the rules and structures the Gangrel has to obey in this circumstance because that's the way it is. Or heck. . . my Crossover Chronicle started, after the individual character's Preludes, with the Geist being picked up by two Internal Affairs agents who were Carthian ghouls and driving to the Carthian meeting because they wanted to ask her some pointed questions about some vampires she'd helped kill during her Prelude. And in recompense for that, she had to help them out with another small matter. It was really just a way of me getting a Mage, a Vampire, and a Geist (and later, a Promethean) in the same room so I could start running a semi-coherent game, but a Gangrel player under similar circumstances would be rather disadvantaged.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That, though, sounds less like something a real vampire would actually want or do and more like something a crazy old guy guy who lived during &quot;King and his Court&quot; time would impose on people because nobody else could possible beat him in a test of power. In other words, for Masquerade, where those insane, un-topple-able power structures were obnoxious and stifling for players. They literally couldn't advance. Ever. Because they couldn't ever match that guy's generation or his thousand years of experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, like I said, I haven't put a lot of thought into it because my players never showed interest in working with the Invictus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853756#post853756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, how to mechanize that?<br /> <br /> I think, for me, this is going to run into issues. I suspect I call for many fewer rolls than others do, and when something does call for rolls, I probably use way more, because I resolve things by task, so each individual piece gets a roll, rather than resolving the conflict in one go. Number of rolls is also just so variable...it seems like it will either never happen or always happen, and it'll really just be the flavor text stuff making Gangrel feel like they ought to. I don't know, I'll consider it. I do like the direction, though, still, just having trouble with the execution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not really sure my own self how to work it mechanically just yet. If you think of something, let me know, and I'll do the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":831,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","user":"ErikModi","date":". 03-26-2016, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T22:29:10-07:00","id":853906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853779#post853779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to chime in to point out that rolling Intimidation is not determining how intimidating you are. It's determining whether or not you succeed at intimidating someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>To you, sure, and that's fine, run it as you like. But to me, Intimidation is determining how you do, and then they react as they actually would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853792#post853792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought WoD (even as far back as VtM) was more story-focused than anything else. You <i>could</i> play it like D&amp;D (kick down the door, kill the &quot;monsters,&quot; take their stuff so you can kick in a bigger door and kill bigger monsters), but that wasn't the way it was designed to be played. Curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see. That's because the opposite of &quot;story game&quot; as I'm using it isn't &quot;dungeon crawl&quot; or &quot;hack and slash.&quot; The difference is, for lack of the better term, simulation, I guess. My games are absolutely not kick in the door action games, no way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853792#post853792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you also seem to be saying that a person with a gun to someone else's head and a clear willingness to use it automatically succeeds at Intimidate checks. That seems wrong to me, somehow. If that's not what you mean, then I apologize for continued derailment.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I just don't think that calls for a roll at all. Slightly different. It's not an automatic success, it's no roll required.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853792#post853792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, are you saying that you can still fail at the goal you set for yourself with a roll even if you succeeded a lot?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if you took an action that does not accomplish said goal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853792#post853792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think the &quot;rich people are bad guys&quot; trope is still alive and well in the modern day, precisely because they're so out-of-touch with the experiences of most people, and are still doing everything they can to build on what they have at the expense of &quot;the lower orders.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but I don't think we picture those people at slick parties in ball rooms anymore, we more think of them drinking smoothies every morning made of $400 &quot;moondust,&quot; at a ranch shooting caviar tins off a fence post, or maybe, at the fanciest, at a country club talking about how the poor should just get jobs running one of their daddy's oversea holdings if they need more money. They're the bad guys, but not because they earned it by being sharks, because they had it handed to them and they use what they have like clueless/selfish asshats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853792#post853792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds awesome, and I'd definitely like to hear more!</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Minneapolis and St. Paul are very, ridiculously cold. As such, the city has very few homeless or street walking prostitutes. There are heated walkways most places and car services for drunks. The few people walking outside are going to be in heavy coats, scarves, and hats. All of this combines to make feeding a real issue. You can't be a lazy feeder and just grab a hobo or a drunk in a bar alley. You have to be very careful and stick to a plan, probably get a herd, etc. So, that's the premise that sets everything else up. Blood supply is way more important than in other cities.<br /> <br /> The Twin Cities area is heavily Nordic in heritage, and the Scandanavian immigrants shoved the local Amerindians out. In my version of the cities, this was paralleled by vampires. The old school Viking vampires that arrived shoved the native Ojibwe and Lakota vampires to the side and took over. The cult of Thor, which functions basically as a branch of the Circle of the Crone, have a great deal of influence because they hold of Horn of Thor (from the myth where Thor is tasked with draining a horn faster than his giant host, but it turns out to be secretly connected to the ocean). The Horn is used as part of a special ritual the cult has developed that causes it to overflow with blood.<br /> <br /> St. Paul and Minneapolis each have their own Princes and vie for the favor of the Cult in order to gain control of the Horn and easy access to blood and blessings for the year. Most vampires in the cities swear fealty to the Prince (or down the chain from him) and become part of an ongoing contest. The Cult created a shell corporation to represent this favor, and there are complex rules about how these shares are given out and acquired. Each year, whichever city has the most shares, gets the cult to move into their city and provide blessings and access to the Horn of Thor with its seemingly infinite blood. Over the course of each year, they run Viking raids on each other, which take many, many forms. You can count coup on/otherwise capture the other city's vampires to earn shares as weregild, or make contacts/allies/blackmail/etc., in the opposing city and then trade that influence for shares, win festival events, etc., etc. It's complicated, way too complicated to explain here in brief, but you get the gist.<br /> <br /> There is a strong tradition of German Lutherans in St. Paul as well, and so, their city is influenced as well by a group of Lancea Sanctum vampires. They are basically converted from the Cult of Thor. They take part in the Viking game but are secretly trying to undermine the Cult of Thor's influence and make everyone vie, instead, for their favor. Meanwhile, the Ojibwe and Lakota vampires never really went away, they just went underground. They kept up their medicine lodges, but did so in secret. Not being/refusing to be a part of the cult of Thor, they've found their own way to deal with the blood shortage. They've developed, essentially, coils of the dragon, and mimic the Ordo Dracul to a small degree. I even worked on a 2e conversion of the 1e Coil of Blood. It's been a while, though, I'd have to find my notes. They pretend to join in on the Viking stuff, but they really hate it, and want to ultimately tear it all down. But the Cult of Thor is their first target.<br /> <br /> In other words, two cities war with each other to gain the favor of a third party while each has a different corrupting influence from within trying to remove that third party entirely. I really like the idea, personally, but I never finished working it all out because the PCs ultimately chose to play in Vancouver instead (I pitched them half a dozen city concepts initially and let them choose).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853792#post853792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they gather together to they can talk to someone, anyone, with whom they have some vague shared (un)life experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't think that requires parties...I think it can be done just fine in much smaller groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2698,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","user":"The Storyteller","date":".  Extra information 03-27-2016, 02:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T02:50:56-07:00","id":853951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853792#post853792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you also seem to be saying that a person with a gun to someone else's head and a clear willingness to use it automatically succeeds at Intimidate checks. That seems wrong to me, somehow. If that's not what you mean, then I apologize for continued derailment.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not wrong, this is a tipical &quot;forcing doors&quot; maneuver. It should remove a door and give bonus dice to the intimidation roll for the gun. Not an automatic success cause someone with hig resolve and composure could don't belive your character will use it or he could simply not be willing to betray his lover (for instance) even if threatened with death (if the roll fail).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:25:28-07:00","id":854054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853951#post853951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not wrong, this is a tipical &quot;forcing doors&quot; maneuver. It should remove a door and give bonus dice to the intimidation roll for the gun. Not an automatic success cause someone with hig resolve and composure could don't belive your character will use it or he could simply not be willing to betray his lover (for instance) even if threatened with death (if the roll fail).</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly using the Doors system, you are correct. I don't use that. I find it silly that someone with a high resolve could &quot;successfully&quot; not believe your threat, even if you are totally serious about it, or that he might refuse to betray someone/something he doesn't care that much about. Those outcomes don't follow logically.<br /> <br /> If you offer a deal that the other guy would like, it is absurd to me that he'd refuse it just because you failed a roll. Or rather, it is absurd that you would need to roll. The guy would just agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T09:36:58-07:00","id":854083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853906#post853906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I just don't think that calls for a roll at all. Slightly different. It's not an automatic success, it's no roll required.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853906#post853906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but I don't think we picture those people at slick parties in ball rooms anymore, we more think of them drinking smoothies every morning made of $400 &quot;moondust,&quot; at a ranch shooting caviar tins off a fence post, or maybe, at the fanciest, at a country club talking about how the poor should just get jobs running one of their daddy's oversea holdings if they need more money. They're the bad guys, but not because they earned it by being sharks, because they had it handed to them and they use what they have like clueless/selfish asshats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what aesthetics you prefer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853906#post853906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Minneapolis and St. Paul are very, ridiculously cold. As such, the city has very few homeless or street walking prostitutes. There are heated walkways most places and car services for drunks. The few people walking outside are going to be in heavy coats, scarves, and hats. All of this combines to make feeding a real issue. You can't be a lazy feeder and just grab a hobo or a drunk in a bar alley. You have to be very careful and stick to a plan, probably get a herd, etc. So, that's the premise that sets everything else up. Blood supply is way more important than in other cities.<br /> <br /> The Twin Cities area is heavily Nordic in heritage, and the Scandanavian immigrants shoved the local Amerindians out. In my version of the cities, this was paralleled by vampires. The old school Viking vampires that arrived shoved the native Ojibwe and Lakota vampires to the side and took over. The cult of Thor, which functions basically as a branch of the Circle of the Crone, have a great deal of influence because they hold of Horn of Thor (from the myth where Thor is tasked with draining a horn faster than his giant host, but it turns out to be secretly connected to the ocean). The Horn is used as part of a special ritual the cult has developed that causes it to overflow with blood.<br /> <br /> St. Paul and Minneapolis each have their own Princes and vie for the favor of the Cult in order to gain control of the Horn and easy access to blood and blessings for the year. Most vampires in the cities swear fealty to the Prince (or down the chain from him) and become part of an ongoing contest. The Cult created a shell corporation to represent this favor, and there are complex rules about how these shares are given out and acquired. Each year, whichever city has the most shares, gets the cult to move into their city and provide blessings and access to the Horn of Thor with its seemingly infinite blood. Over the course of each year, they run Viking raids on each other, which take many, many forms. You can count coup on/otherwise capture the other city's vampires to earn shares as weregild, or make contacts/allies/blackmail/etc., in the opposing city and then trade that influence for shares, win festival events, etc., etc. It's complicated, way too complicated to explain here in brief, but you get the gist.<br /> <br /> There is a strong tradition of German Lutherans in St. Paul as well, and so, their city is influenced as well by a group of Lancea Sanctum vampires. They are basically converted from the Cult of Thor. They take part in the Viking game but are secretly trying to undermine the Cult of Thor's influence and make everyone vie, instead, for their favor. Meanwhile, the Ojibwe and Lakota vampires never really went away, they just went underground. They kept up their medicine lodges, but did so in secret. Not being/refusing to be a part of the cult of Thor, they've found their own way to deal with the blood shortage. They've developed, essentially, coils of the dragon, and mimic the Ordo Dracul to a small degree. I even worked on a 2e conversion of the 1e Coil of Blood. It's been a while, though, I'd have to find my notes. They pretend to join in on the Viking stuff, but they really hate it, and want to ultimately tear it all down. But the Cult of Thor is their first target.<br /> <br /> In other words, two cities war with each other to gain the favor of a third party while each has a different corrupting influence from within trying to remove that third party entirely. I really like the idea, personally, but I never finished working it all out because the PCs ultimately chose to play in Vancouver instead (I pitched them half a dozen city concepts initially and let them choose).</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds fascinating. Though, it really isn't THAT cold here most of the year. Late December through early February tend to be the worst, but even then, 0 degrees F with a -40 wind chill are rare, except in the harshest of winters. There's plenty of people about on the streets in the right areas, even at night (though the number is less than in the summer.) Still, sounds pretty awesome on the whole. And Lutherans are all over, not just St. Paul, and we have plenty of other Christian denominations as well. We're kind of at the north end of the Bible Belt, and while fairly liberal, it's not hard to find some real religious conservatives. On the whole, I love it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853906#post853906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't think that requires parties...I think it can be done just fine in much smaller groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, depends on the aesthetics, and how willing the higher ups are to meet with random newbies. If you're some two-days-dead, unknown vampire, it's not likely you'll get a chance to meet any of the movers and shakers of the city unless you can run into them at some kind of large social gathering. Which means, for new PCs, the only way they'll learn about the political situation is through second, third, or fourth-hand information. Which can certainly be an interesting way to play things, but drastically increases the amount of work the ST has to go through creating all the various &quot;tiers&quot; of go-betweens from the leadership on down. So I think most tend to make it easier on themselves and their players (remembering who all these people are is rough, and time spent taking notes on what was just said is time not listening to what is being said) by having fairly regular large social events where the brand new can rub elbows with the incomprehensibly old. Not that big social gatherings are the only thing vampires ever do, but that it's something that happens on a regular basis. Less frequent than feeding, more frequent than torpor.<br /> <br /> The Covenants themselves are basically excuses to socialize. The Invictus and Carthians likely have some kind of governmental meeting every night, whether this is a &quot;closed session&quot; where they decide things or an &quot;open session&quot; where anyone who wants can attend and air grievances depends on how many shits that particular incarnation gives about their people. The Lancea Sanctum should have &quot;church services&quot; at least once a week, with anyone and everyone allowed, if not encouraged, to attend. Likewise, the Circle would get together on about a weekly basis to practice their religion. The Ordo is likely to be the outlier here, as they're just as likely to endorse private research as they are mass brainstorming session and &quot;scientific&quot; conferences to discuss and evaluate new ideas. And of course, larger and more open meetings means more chances to recruit new members, perhaps even from other Covenants, strengthening that Covenant's position relative to the others. The &quot;real&quot; business may only get done behind closed doors, but everyone wants to see and be seen and at least pretend they get to participate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T10:07:05-07:00","id":854090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=854054#post854054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly using the Doors system, you are correct. I don't use that. I find it silly that someone with a high resolve could &quot;successfully&quot; not believe your threat, even if you are totally serious about it, or that he might refuse to betray someone/something he doesn't care that much about. Those outcomes don't follow logically.<br /> <br /> If you offer a deal that the other guy would like, it is absurd to me that he'd refuse it just because you failed a roll. Or rather, it is absurd that you would need to roll. The guy would just agree.</div> </div> </div> </div>The roll come up just in some situations. I mean: if you point a gun and ask for the wallet, ok, no roll is needed. If you ask to betray your mother or your lover, I would go for the roll. Someone that can see the esitation in your eyes or the uncertainty in your voice could also try to disarm you or hold on on his position. If otherwise he sees in you madness and resolution could take your threats more seriously.<br /> The bonus given by the gun (maybe +3 on the roll) and a door away, is a good one to represent your rised dangerousness in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T14:27:44-07:00","id":854668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=853906#post853906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To you, sure, and that's fine, run it as you like. But to me, Intimidation is determining how you do, and then they react as they actually would.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't ever 'do' Intimidate RAW, you do actions that use the Intimidate skill.<br /> <br /> So, the Intimidate example for an interegation is a contested action, meaning the target rolls as well. This represents their ability to not be intimidated, and overall how well the attempt works as intended by the player. Do you roll intimidation checks as non-contested, non-resisted since its just a measure of how intimidating the PC is without any reflection of the NPC involved?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T07:12:37-07:00","id":855056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane?p=854090#post854090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The roll come up just in some situations. I mean: if you point a gun and ask for the wallet, ok, no roll is needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. I remember hearing in line in passing (think it was from some Law and Order incarnation or other) where a known hold-up artist was explaining that he couldn't have shot the victim of the week, because he uses a hand cannon while the victim was shot with a 9mm. He explains that he uses a really big caliber gun because &quot;some people are stupid enough to argue with a 9 mil.&quot; Even if you've got a gun, someone might be brave enough or stupid enough to not give in, or might have something in their wallet that they feel is worth dying for. Think back to Ghost, where Sam the Stock Broker was perfectly willing to hand over the cash in his wallet, but refused to hand over the wallet itself because it had sensitive information for his entire company's fortune in it (which is why he was being robbed in the first place.)<br /> <br /> The motivations of the NPC are just as important at the motivations of the PC. The NPC might be answering to someone even scarier. A guy with a loaded gun to your head can only kill you, a Nosferatu with Nightmare can make you live in an eternal hell, and a Ventrue with Dominate can make you murder your own family. They might be clinging to whatever code of honor or ethics they have that tell them not be a rat. They may just be a contrary asshole who gets more resolved to deny something the more someone else obviously wants it. Quite simply, there should be no such thing as a guaranteed success as soon as another character, Player or Non, gets involved. Every attempt to get someone else to do what you want should have a chance, no matter how slim, to fail. Stating that &quot;under X circumstance, there is no logical way this cannot work&quot; is a fallacy, because humans are fundamentally illogical. Even in real life, threats of violence and torture (or actual violence and torture) don't always yield the desired results. Human beings are complex animals, their reactions are not always predictable, and responses to stimuli can vary greatly even within the same individual.<br /> <br /> But this is getting increasingly off topic. I'd suggest, if we have more to say on the topic of Intimidation rolls and so forth, someone start a new thread to talk about it, because this has nothing to do with Gangrel Clan Weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:28:36-07:00","id":855085,"title":"","content":"Basically I agree with you. Mine was just an example of something I wouldn't roll if it isn't important for the game. But, yes, as said, in a general situation I agree with you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T15:05:06-07:00","id":908645,"title":"","content":"Hy, storytellers!<br /> <br /> I've been reading your posts, and I think that finally found a houserule for the Gangrel's weakness good enough to my group. <br /> <br /> The Feral Curse<br /> <br /> &quot;Gangrel Beasts boil close to the surface. A Gangrel can run with the devil inside her, but has difficulty fighting it. All her dice pools to resist frenzy related to hungry or thread are limited by her Humanity dots. This weakness does not affect dice pools to ride the wave, or frenzy estimulated by fire or sunlight. As well, the predator within calls for a prey, so, everytime when a Gangrel feed using the Kiss - instead of the Assault - she gains no nourishment from the first few vitae taken . This amount is equal to (10 \u2013 Humanity).&quot;<br /> <br /> That's it. Now we have Gangrel characters encouraged to act like the predators they are. Or they will frighten their victims terribly, as Eli from &quot;Let Me In/ Let The Right One In&quot; (a true gangrel to me), or exhaust them almost completely seeking to satiate their hunger predator, as Lestat (Interview with the Vampire, the only book in which he does not look like a superhero, but a unforgettable degenerate character).<br /> <br /> Changing the topic a little, I think the Ventrue's weakness also has issues, looking soft compared to the anothers. so I developed some house rules ideas for them too. Soon as I can, I will post it here.<br /> <br /> After all, I must apologize for my bad bad english, cause I'm brazilian, and everything that I learned was on my own,<br /> <br /> Thanks for sharing ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11934-draugr","name":"Draugr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11934_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T02:53:10-07:00","id":909006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/849587-fixing-what-i-dislike-about-the-gangrel-clan-bane#post849587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> <br /> The Gangrel flaw is just not to my preference. The Gangrel are supposed to be wild and bestial, but their flaw, the way you avoid it, is by doing exactly the opposite of that, by maintaining humanity, avoiding anger and anger inducing situations, being extremely polite and nice to everyone to avoid provocations, feeding carefully to keep from hunger, etc., etc. It's everything a Gangrel shouldn't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense, but I think there are two things you've missed in your reasoning:<br /> <br /> 1. Every clan bane is linked to Humanity in some way, and thus maintaining high Humanity is a way for everyone to avoid or mitigate their bane. The Gangrel aren't exceptional in this regard.<br /> <br /> 2. Gangrel bane caps their frenzy dice pools, but not their Riding the Wave pools. Hence, the way to avoid the bane without taking the moral high road and maintaining high Humanity is to ride the wave as often as possible. Going this route, you end up with a character that frenzies more often than other vampires (because she rides the wave where other vamps would have just suppressed the frenzy) but with less random side effects (because she frenzies on her own terms), creating the impression the character is more in tune with her Beast. Isn't this exactly what you want out of clan banes - avoiding them by embodying them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T02:40:08-07:00","id":938001,"title":"","content":"Hi storyteller, I too been thinking about how to improve the bane and here is my take:<br /> <br /> To my mind, Gangrel are supposed to be wild and free, like animals. One of the easiest way to distinguish animals from humans is the use of tools. Too me, this include indirect means of solving problems like social maneuvering, example:<br /> <br /> A gangrel is more likely to fight someone with his bare hands than with a knife or a gun. He is more likely too turn into an animal and ran than hijack a car. He is also less likely to turn for allies and contacts as a way to solve problems or find somebody. If he need somone found he'll track it himself, or use his pack of animals. He is more prone to have hunting grounds than a herd which he'll have to interract.<br /> <br /> So, here is my idea, taking a bit of inspiration from the carthin pull merit, we shuold limit the use of tools, in game terms this means equipment like weapons, vehicles, libraries, etc. Also, merits like allies, contacts, herd, resources and social maneuvering.<br /> <br /> If we tie this to humanity, its starts to look promising. Lets say a gangrel can only make use of this tools (equipment, merits, etc) a number of times per week equal to his humanity, with this restrictions he would start to act more wild and direct. Why waste your few social interactions on some nobody when you could just beat him up and make him tell you whay you want. <br /> <br /> Now, what happens if he exceeds this limit is of course a condition. Here we have more options, I like a blood potency penalty to resist frenzy for a number of nights equal to twice his blood potency, needing to spend a willpower and getting an additional -1 for each time he incurs in the restricted behavior.<br /> <br /> This model stills need work. I thought that evrry time the character attempts to use social maneuvering on an other this should count as an use for porpuses of the bane. But more precisely, it only counts the number of people to wich you attempt this. If your humanity is 6 you can social manuver six diferent people as much as you want. I know you are not a fan of social manuvering but you could find a way to make it work.<br /> <br /> The other equipment like weapons, cars, libraries, crowbars, etc, would need another time distinction like a night, scene or just like social m, every diferent tool count as one.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I believe this is a start, still needs calibration, need the opinion of others, I'd been told I'm a harsh storyteller. However I believe this is in line with our objectives. A gangrel will become an animal lest he turn into a monstrous beast.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12173-basilistik","name":"Basilistik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T04:49:14-07:00","id":938026,"title":"","content":"Forcing all characters not even into a clan stereotype, but the most exaggerated, extreme subset of it, is not how clan banes are supposed to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}